hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9001","8974 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Israil narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: Whoever establishes the prayer but does not give the zakat has no prayer."
"9002","8975 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Khulaydah, that Abdullah came to him while he had set up furnishings in his house. Abdullah said: Lighten the furnishings of your house, for the people are about to become people of the packsaddle."
"9003","8976 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Awn ibn Abdullah, he said: Abdullah said: The believer is sociable, and there is no good in one who neither befriends nor is befriended."
"9004","8977 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, al-Masudi narrated, (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Awn ibn Abdullah, that Abdullah used to seek refuge from four, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from wealth that makes me transgress, from poverty that makes me forget, from desire that destroys me, and from a deed that grieves me."
"9005","8978 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Awn, that Abdullah used to say: Beware of difficult speech."
"9006","8979 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, al-Masudi narrated, (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Awn, he said: Abdullah said to his companions when they came to him: Do you sit together? They said: We do not abandon that. He said: Do you visit one another? They said: Yes, O Abu Abd al-Rahman; a man among us misses his brother and walks in search of him to the far end of Kufa until he meets him. He said: You will remain in good as long as you do that."
"9007","8980 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad narrated, from Ubayd ibn Abi al-Jad, from Qays ibn Sakan, from Abdullah, he said: Do not eat of cheese except what the Muslims and the People of the Book make."
"9008","8981 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, from Abu Ubaydah, that Abdullah, when he stood in prayer, lowered therein his voice, his hand, and his gaze."
"9009","8982 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, from al-Masudi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, he said: Abdullah never addressed a sermon in Kufa except that I attended it. I heard him one day when he was asked about a man who divorces eight times and the like of that, and he said: It is as he said. Then he said: Allah, Exalted and Mighty, sent down His Book and made its exposition clear; whoever approaches the matter from its proper side, it has been made clear to him; and whoever opposes, then by Allah, we cannot bear all your opposition."
"9010","8983 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shubah narrated, Yahya ibn Amr ibn Salamah said: He informed me from his father, he said: Ibn Masud was asked about fasting for a lifetime and he disliked it, and said: Fasting three days of every month."
"9011","8984 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Yahya ibn Amr ibn Salamah, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: Fasting three days of every month removes the rancor of the chest."
"9012","8985 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from al-Hakam, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: Abdullah used to say after bowing: O Allah, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything besides, O Possessor of praise and glory; none withholds what You give and none gives what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You."
"9013","8986 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Wail ibn Rabiah, from Ibn Masud, he said: Between the heaven and the earth is a journey of five hundred years."
"9014","8987 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, that he said: Between the lowest heaven and the one above it is a journey of five hundred years, and between every two heavens is a journey of five hundred years, and between the seventh heaven and the Kursi is a journey of five hundred years, and between the Kursi and the water is a journey of five hundred years; and the Throne is upon the water, and Allah, Exalted and Mighty, is upon the Throne, knowing what you are upon."
"9015","8988 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The sun rises from Jahannam between the two horns of Satan, and between the two horns of Satan; whenever it rises into the sky by a morsel, a gate of the gates of the Fire is opened; and when the heat intensifies, all its gates are opened."
"9016","8989 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Ammar, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: Abdullah saw some dirhams with a man and said: What will you do with them? He said: I shall buy with them a firq of ghee. He said: Give them to your wife to place under her bedding, then buy meat every day for a dirham."
"9017","8990 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah, he said: Allah, Exalted and Mighty, apportioned among you your characters as He apportioned among you your provisions; and Allah gives wealth to whom He loves and to whom He does not love, but He gives faith only to whom He loves. So if Allah loves a servant, He gives him faith. Whoever is stingy with wealth to spend it, and fears the enemy to fight him, and the night to endure it, let him say much: there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great, and praise be to Allah, and glory be to Allah."
"9018","8991 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wail, he said: Abdullah said: Do you know how Islam decreases? They said: As the dye of a garment fades, and as a beast wears down, and as the dirham tarnishes from long keeping. He said: That is indeed part of it, and greater than that is the death, or going, of the scholars."
"9019","8992 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Sirat is placed over the even surface of Jahannam like the edge of a sharpened sword, slippery and causing to slip; upon it are hooks of fire by which people are snatched. Some are held and fall into it, and some are struck down; and among them is one who passes like lightning, and it is not long before he is saved; then like the wind, and it is not long before he is saved; then like the running of a horse, then like the striving of a man, then like the trotting of a man, then like the walking of a man; until the last of them is a man whom the Fire has scorched and who has met evil therein, until Allah admits him to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy. It is said to him: Wish and ask. He says: My Lord, do You mock me while You are the Lord of Might? It is said to him: Wish and ask. He said: Until, when his wishes are exhausted, he says: For you is what you asked, and the like of it with it. He said: And Abu Salih narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: And tenfold of it with it."
"9020","8993 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri and Mamar, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, he said: A man from Bajilah came to Abdullah and said: I have married a virgin slave-girl, and I fear she will dislike me. Abdullah said: Affection is from Allah, and dislike is from Satan, to make him hate what Allah made lawful for him. When you go in to her, command her to pray behind you two rakahs. Al-Amash said: I mentioned it to Ibrahim, and he said: Abdullah said: And say: O Allah, bless me in my family and bless them in me; O Allah, provide me from them and provide them from me; O Allah, join us together as long as You join us to good, and separate us when You separate us to good."
"9021","8994 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, that a man came to Ibn Masud and said: I have married a woman, and I fear dislike. He said: When you come to her, pray two rakahs and say: O Allah, bless me in my family and bless them in me; O Allah, join us together as long as You join us in good, and separate us when You separate us to good."
"9022","8995 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from more than one of his companions, from Ibn Masud, he said: It may be that a man says: Allah commanded such and forbade such, and Allah, Exalted and Mighty, says to him: You lied; or he says: Allah prohibited such and permitted such, and Allah says to him: You lied."
"9023","8996 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Shubah narrated, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah, he said: The parable of one who persists in prayer is like one who knocks at a door; and whoever keeps knocking at a door is likely to have it opened for him."
"9024","8997 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Zubayd, from Murrah, he said: Abdullah said: As long as you are in prayer, you are knocking at the door of the King; and whoever knocks much at the door of the King is likely to have it opened for him."
"9025","8998 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Mansur, from Zubayd, from Murrah ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, he said: The excellence of night prayer over day prayer is like the excellence of secret charity over open charity."
"9026","8999 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Zubayd, from Murrah, he said: Abdullah said: The excellence of night prayer over day prayer is like the excellence of secret charity over open charity."
"9027","9000 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: Abdullah said: The master of the months is Ramadan, and the master of the days is Friday."
"9028","9001 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: Abdullah recited this verse: {On the Day the earth is changed to other than the earth, and the heavens, and they come forth to Allah, the One, the Irresistible}. He said: An earth is brought as if it were an ingot of silver upon which no blood was shed and upon which no sin was done; and the first matter judged among the people therein is blood."
"9029","9002 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Muslim al-Batin, from Abu al-Ubaydayn, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The awwah is the merciful."
"9030","9003 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Karim, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: {Indeed Ibrahim was awwah, forbearing}. He said: The awwah is the merciful."
"9031","9004 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: Ibn Masud was asked about the awwah? He said: He is the supplicating one."
"9032","9005 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated, al-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated, from Yusuf ibn Sad, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud used to narrate every day in the mosque; and when Thursday came, the people of the outlying districts and villages attended him. A blind man came and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is the awwah? He said: The merciful. He said: What is squandering? He said: What is spent in other than right. He said: What is al-maun? He said: What the people share among themselves, meaning loans of utensils."
"9033","9006 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Shubah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, that a man called Abu al-Ubaydayn - and he was a blind man - and Abdullah ibn Masud used to honor him, asked him about al-maun, and he said: The axe and the bucket - or he said: The axe and the pot - and he asked him about squandering, and he said: Spending wealth in other than its lawful place; and he asked him about the awwah, he said: The merciful."
"9034","9007 - al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Abu al-Ubaydayn al-Amiri - and he was blind in sight, and Abdullah ibn Masud used to show him kindness - and he said to Abdullah: Whom shall we ask if we do not ask you? Abdullah took pity on him and said: He said: What is the awwah? He said: The merciful. He said: What is the ummah? He said: One who teaches good. He said: What is the qanit? He said: The obedient. He said: What is al-maun? He said: What the people share among themselves. He said: What is squandering? He said: Spending wealth in other than its right."
"9035","9008 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Salamah, from Muslim al-Batin, from Abu al-Ubaydayn, he said: Abdullah was asked about squandering? He said: Spending in other than right."
"9036","9009 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Abu Waki narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ubaydayn, he said: I asked Abdullah about His saying: {And do not squander wastefully}. He said: It is spending in other than right."
"9037","9010 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ubaydayn and Sad ibn Iyad, from Abdullah, he said: We, the companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say that al-maun is: the bucket, the pot, and the axe, which cannot be dispensed with."
"9038","9011 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: {Al-maun}. He said: The axe, the pot, and the bucket."
"9039","9012 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, concerning His saying: {And withhold al-maun}. He said: It is wealth whose right is not given. I said: Ibn Masud says: It is what the people pass among themselves of good. He said: That is what I tell you."
"9040","9013 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, he said: Every kindness is charity; and we used to count al-maun in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as lending the bucket, the pot, and the like of that."
"9041","9014 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Shayban narrated, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: We used to count al-maun as the axe, the pot, and the bucket."
"9042","9015 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Khaythamah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {Indeed the hypocrites are in the lowest depth of the Fire}. He said: Chests of iron closed upon them."
"9043","9016 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {A settlement and a repository}. He said: The settlement is the womb, and the repository is the earth in which he dies."
"9044","9017 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: Its repository is in this world, and its settlement is in the womb."
"9045","9018 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {And of cattle, beasts of burden and small ones}. He said: The beasts of burden are what carries loads of camels, and the farsh are the small ones."
"9046","9019 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {Do they await except that the angels come to them, or your Lord comes, or some signs of your Lord come; on the Day some signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before}. He said: The rising of the sun along with the moon from its west, like two hobbled camels."
"9047","9020 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {On the Day some signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith}. He said: The rising of the sun from its west."
"9048","9021 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Sharik, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated, from Sad ibn Iyad, from Ibn Masud, His saying: {And do not squander wastefully}. He said: Spending in other than its right."
"9049","9022 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: al-Firyabi narrated, from Sufyan, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Zirr, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {There is no blame upon them to lay aside their garments, not displaying adornment}. He said: The outer cloak."
"9050","9023 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, he said: We asked Abdullah about this verse: {And do not think those killed in the way of Allah} up to {they are provided}. He said: The souls of the martyrs are with Allah, Exalted and Mighty, like green birds having lamps hung from the Throne, roaming in Paradise wherever they wish. He said: Your Lord looked upon them a look and said: Do you desire anything that I may increase you? They said: Our Lord, do we not roam in Paradise wherever we wish in it? He said: Then He looked upon them a second time and said: Do you desire anything that I may increase you? They said: Our Lord, do we not roam in Paradise wherever we wish in it? Then He looked to them a third time and said: Do you desire anything that I may increase you? They said: Return our souls to our bodies that we may fight in Your way and be killed another time. He said: Then He remained silent from them."
"9051","9024 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, he said: We asked Abdullah ibn Masud about this verse: {And do not think those killed in the way of Allah are dead; rather alive with their Lord, provided}. He said: We had asked about it. He said: The souls of the martyrs are like green birds. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Thawri."
"9052","9025 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said in the third: He said: Do you desire anything that I may increase you? They said: Convey our greeting to our Prophet from us, and inform him that we are pleased and He is pleased with us."
"9053","9026 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Misar ibn Kidam narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Ibn Sabit, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {Its fuel is men and stones}. He said: Stones of brimstone which Allah, Exalted and Mighty, makes with Him as He wills and as He wills."
"9054","9027 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Suddi, Abu Sad al-Azdi narrated to me, from Abu al-Kanud, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {And say: Hittah}. He said: They said: Wheat, a red grain containing barley; and that is His saying: {So those who wronged changed a word other than what was said to them}."
"9055","9028 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {So whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him; and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him}. He said: He is forgiven."
"9056","9029 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: These verses from the end of al-Baqarah were sent down: {The Messenger believed} from a treasure beneath the Throne."
"9057","9030 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Hushaym narrated, Juwaybir informed us, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Masud, {And whether you disclose what is in yourselves or conceal it}. He said: It was abrogated by the verse after it: {For it is what it earned, and upon it is what it acquired}."
"9058","9031 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: This path is attended; the devils attend it, saying: O servants of Allah, this is the road. So hold fast to the rope of Allah, for the straight path is the Book of Allah."
"9059","9032 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Jami ibn Abi Rashid, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: {And hold fast to the rope of Allah all together}. Abdullah said: The Quran."
"9060","9033 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Hushaym narrated, al-Awwam informed us, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Masud, he said: The rope of Allah, Exalted and Mighty, is the community."
"9061","9034 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {Those who remember Allah standing and sitting and upon their sides}. He said: If you cannot pray standing, then sitting; and if not, then lying down."
"9062","9035 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, they said: Abdullah said: In the Book of Allah there are two verses; no servant commits a sin then recites them and seeks Allah's forgiveness except that Allah forgives him: {And those who, when they commit an indecency or wrong themselves, remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins - and who forgives sins except Allah} and His saying: {And whoever does evil or wrongs himself, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, will find Allah Forgiving, Merciful}."
"9063","9036 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Ali and Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {And married women except what your right hands possess}. Ali said: The polytheist women, when captured, become lawful for him. And Ibn Masud said: The polytheist and the Muslim women."
"9064","9037 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Sufyan, from Jabir, from al-Qasim or al-Shabi, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {And the companion at side}. He said: The wife."
"9065","9038 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Suddi, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: {And We shall surely make them taste the nearer punishment}. He said: The Day of Badr; and the greater punishment, perhaps they return. He said: Whoever remains among them, that he repent and return."
"9066","9039 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Qays, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: It is indeed written in the Torah: For those whose sides forsake their beds, what no eye has seen, and no ear has heard, and what never occurred to the heart of a mortal; and indeed it is in the Quran: {No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort of eyes}."
"9067","9040 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, he said: The dung beetle is indeed punished in its hole for the sins of the children of Adam. Then he recited: {And if Allah were to take men for what they earned, He would not leave upon its back any creature}."
"9068","9041 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {By those ranged in rows} He said: The angels. {Then the drivers driving} He said: The angels. {Then the reciters of remembrance} He said: The angels."
"9069","9042 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Ibn Masud, he said: In the seven heavens there is a heaven in which there is not a handspan place except upon it is the forehead of an angel or his two feet, standing. Then he recited: {And indeed we are the ranged ones, and indeed we are the glorifiers}."
"9070","9043 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah: {And he overcame me in speech}. He said: Dawud did no more than say: {Entrust it to me}."
"9071","9044 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {Our Lord, You made us die twice and gave us life twice}. He said: It is like the one in al-Baqarah: {And you were dead, then He gave you life, then He will make you die, then He will give you life, then to Him you are returned}."
"9072","9045 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, the like of the hadith of Israil."
"9073","9046 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, he said: We were sitting in the mosque when a man came to us narrating. He said: On the Day of Resurrection a smoke will come and seize the ears of the hypocrites, and seize the believers like the semblance of a cold. So we went to Abdullah ibn Masud and told him while he was reclining, and he sat up and said: O people, whoever knows knowledge, let him speak of it; and whoever does not know, let him say: Allah knows best. For it is part of a man's knowledge to say of what he does not know: Allah knows best. Allah said to His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: {Say: I do not ask you for it any reward, and I am not of the affected}. And I shall narrate to you about the smoke: When Quraysh resisted and were slow toward Islam, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against them and said: O Allah, help me against them with seven like the seven of Yusuf. A year of famine struck them until it consumed everything, until they ate carrion and bones, until a man would see between him and the sky smoke. And that is His saying: {So watch for the Day the sky brings a clear smoke, covering the people; this is a painful punishment. Our Lord, remove from us the punishment; indeed we are believers}. So it was removed from them, and they returned to their disbelief; then He seized them on the Day of Badr. And that is His saying: {On the Day We seize with the greatest seizure; indeed We are avengers}. He said: The greatest seizure is the Day of Badr."
"9074","9047 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from al-Amash, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, the like of it."
"9075","9048 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, he said: While a man was narrating in Kindah, he said: A smoke will come on the Day of Resurrection and seize the ears of the hypocrites. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"9076","9049 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated, Muslim ibn Subayh narrated, he said: I heard Masruq saying: Abdullah ibn Masud said: Five have passed: the smoke, the moon, the Romans, the seizure, and the binding."
"9077","9050 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Israil, Abu Ishaq narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord}. He said: That is Jibril, peace be upon him, in a robe of Rafraf, having filled what is between the heaven and the earth."
"9078","9051 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: {He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord}. He said: He saw a green Rafraf that had covered the horizon."
"9079","9052 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb and Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, (ha) and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, they said: Shubah informed us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: {He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord}. He said: He saw a green Rafraf that had covered the horizon of the sky."
"9080","9053 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: {He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord}. He said: Green Rafraf from Paradise that had covered the horizon."
"9081","9054 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord}. He said: Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw Jibril in his form, having six hundred wings, none of them except that it had covered what is between the east and the west."
"9082","9055 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shubah narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr narrated, (ha) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated, (ha) and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to me, Sufyan narrated, all of them, from al-Shaybani, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: {He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord}. He said: He has six hundred wings."
"9083","9056 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Huzayl, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {At the Lote Tree of the Utmost}. He said: The thicket of Paradise; at it were placed palaces of sundus and istabraq."
"9084","9057 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The righteous dream is one part of seventy parts of prophethood; and the scorching wind from which the jinn were created is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Jahannam; and this fire of yours is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Jahannam."
"9085","9058 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Israil, from al-Suddi, from Abu Malik, from Masruq, from Ibn Masud, he said: Coral is red beads."
"9086","9059 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {O you who believed, do not take as allies a people with whom Allah is angry; they have despaired of the Hereafter}. So they do not believe in it nor are they rewarded: this is the disbeliever when he dies and sees his recompense and looks upon it."
"9087","9060 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Sufyan, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, he said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Masud and asked him about this verse: {And whoever is saved from the stinginess of his soul, those are the successful}. I am a man who cannot help that nothing comes out of me, and I fear this verse has befallen me. Abdullah ibn Masud said: You mentioned miserliness, and miserliness is an evil thing; but what Allah mentioned is not what you said. That is that you deliberately take the wealth of another, or the wealth of your brother, and consume it."
"9088","9061 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {Successive}. He said: Consecutive."
"9089","9062 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from Zayd ibn Muawiyah, from Alqamah ibn Qays, Murrah said: From Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {Its seal is musk}. He said: It is not a seal with which it is sealed, but it is mixed with musk. Have you not seen the woman among your women saying: It is mixed of such and such perfume?"
"9090","9063 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah, from Abdullah, concerning al-khunnas {the retreating ones, the sweeping ones}. What is it, O Amr? He said: I said: Cattle. He said: And I hold that."
"9091","9064 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, {And recite to them the story of him to whom We gave Our signs}. He said: He is Balam, and it is said Balam."
"9092","9065 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Farwah, from Murrah, from Abdullah, {You shall surely ride stage upon stage}. He said: The heaven."
"9093","9066 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, both of them, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Rabah, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: I brought to Ibn Masud runaway slaves from Yemen. He said: The reward and the spoil. He said: I said: As for the reward, we have known it; what is the spoil? He said: Forty dirhams from every person."
"9094","9067 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said: Before the Hour there is al-harj. Abu al-Ahwas said: Al-harj is killing."
"9095","9068 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: That for which Yusuf was bought was twenty dirhams; and his family, when he sent to them while they were in Egypt, were ninety-three souls; their men were prophets and their women truthful; and by Allah, they did not go out with him with Musa until they reached six hundred thousand and seventy thousand."
"9096","9069 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Misar, from Man ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, he said: Abdullah said: In al-Nisa there are five verses for which the world and what is in it would not please me in their stead; and I know that the scholars, when they pass them, recognize them: {If you avoid the major sins of what you are forbidden, We shall expiate from you your evil deeds and admit you to a noble entrance} and His saying: {Indeed Allah does not wrong the weight of an atom; and if it be a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward} and {Indeed Allah does not forgive that partners be set up with Him and forgives what is less than that for whom He wills} {And if they, when they wronged themselves, had come to you and sought Allah's forgiveness, and the Messenger had sought forgiveness for them, they would have found Allah Relenting, Merciful} {And whoever does evil or wrongs himself, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, will find Allah Forgiving, Merciful}."
"9097","9070 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Jarir narrated, from Layth, from Abu Hubayrah, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: In the Quran there are two verses; no servant commits a sin, then recites them and seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that He forgives him. They asked him about them, but he did not tell them. Alqamah and al-Aswad, one of them said to his companion: Come with us. They went to the house and took the mushaf and leafed through al-Baqarah and said: We did not see them. Then they took up al-Nisa until they reached this verse: {And whoever does evil or wrongs himself, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, will find Allah Forgiving, Merciful}. He said: This is one. Then they leafed through Al Imran until they reached His saying: {And those who, when they commit an indecency or wrong themselves, remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins - and who forgives sins except Allah - and do not persist in what they did}. They said: This is another. Then they closed the mushaf, then came to Abdullah and said: Are they these two verses? He said: Yes."
"9098","9071 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Jarir narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: A man remains in latitude in his religion as long as he does not shed unlawful blood; and when he sheds unlawful blood, modesty is stripped from him."
"9099","9072 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Khalid narrated, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning the saying of the Exalted and Mighty: {Upon you is yourselves}. He said: This is not its time; say it as long as it is accepted from you; and when it is rejected from you, then upon you is yourselves; whoever strayed will not harm you."
"9100","9073 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, from Husayn, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {The Day of Criterion, the Day the two hosts met}. He said: Badr was on the seventeenth past of Ramadan."
"9101","9074 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the seventeenth gone of Ramadan, the morning of the Day of Badr: {The Day of Criterion, the Day the two hosts met}; and on the twenty-first and on the twenty-third, for it is only in the odd nights."
"9102","9075 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Abdullah said: Recognize the hypocrites by three: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks, and when he covenants he betrays; and Allah sent down its confirmation in His Book: {And among them is one who covenanted with Allah: If He gives us of His bounty} to the end of the verse."
"9103","9076 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Quran and honey are two cures."
"9104","9077 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Hushaym narrated, Mughirah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: {Those whom they call seek to their Lord the means}. He said: There were people worshipping them, then those who were worshipped became Muslim, while those who worshipped them did not know. So Allah, Exalted and Mighty, reproached them with that and said: {Those whom they call seek to their Lord the means}."
"9105","9078 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated, from al-Suddi, from Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {And whoever intends therein deviation with wrong, We shall make him taste a painful punishment}. He said: Whoever intends a sin and does it outside the House, it is not recorded against him until he does it; and whoever intends a sin and does it in the House, Allah will not take him from this world until He makes him taste a painful punishment."
"9106","9079 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Hushaym narrated, Sayyar informed us, from one who narrated to him, that Ibn Masud saw some market people who heard the adhan, left their goods, and rose to prayer. He said: These are those of whom Allah, Exalted and Mighty, said: {Men whom neither trade nor sale diverts from the remembrance of Allah}."
"9107","9080 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, al-Muharibi and Abu Awanah narrated, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Qays ibn al-Sakan, from Abdullah ibn Masud, {And We sent the winds as pollinators}. He said: Allah sends the wind, so it carries water; then a cloud passes and pours as the milch camel pours, then it rains."
"9108","9081 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays narrated, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: I do not compare anything with anything; no foot slips after firmness."
"9109","9082 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Waki narrated, from Salamah ibn Nubayt, from al-Dahhak, that Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, melted silver from the treasury, then sent to the people of the mosque and said: Whoever wishes to look at al-muhl, let him look at this."
"9110","9083 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that he entered the treasury and called for some filings therein, and kindled fire upon them until they melted. He said: Where is the questioner about al-muhl? This is al-muhl."
"9111","9084 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Waki narrated, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, {And there is none of you except will come to it}. He said: Coming to it is the Sirat."
"9112","9085 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Waki narrated, from Abu Sinan Said ibn Sinan, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, he said: It reached Ibn Masud that Marwan says: {And We gave him his family and the like of them with them}. He said: He was given a family other than his family. Ibn Masud said: Rather he was given his family themselves, and the like of them with them."
"9113","9086 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Jarir narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah: {And Dhu al-Nun, when he went off angry}. He said: He is a slave who fled from his master."
"9114","9087 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from one who narrated to him, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: When there remain in the Fire those abiding therein forever, they are placed in coffins of fire containing nails of fire - he said that two or three times - and they see none in the Fire punished but themselves. Then Abdullah recited: {For them therein is sighing, and they therein hear not}."
"9115","9088 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah: {Sons and grandsons}. He said: They are the in-laws."
"9116","9089 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Bukayr al-Tayalisi al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated, Sharik narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The hafadah are the in-laws."
"9117","9090 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, {Sons and grandsons}. He said: They are the in-laws."
"9118","9091 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: Abdullah said to me: Do you know what hafadah is? I said: Yes, they are the grandchildren of a man from his children and his children's children. He said: No, they are the in-laws."
"9119","9092 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: I used to recite the mushaf to Abdullah, and we came to this verse: {And He made for you from your spouses sons and grandsons}. Abdullah said to me: Do you know what al-hafadah is? I said: A man's retinue. He said: No, they are the in-laws."
"9120","9093 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {Sons and grandsons}. He said: The hafadah are the in-laws."
"9121","9094 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: Allah, Exalted and Mighty, indeed supports the religion with the wicked man."
"9122","9095 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: {The journeyers} are the fasting ones."
"9123","9096 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, {And how many a prophet fought, with him great hosts}. He said: Thousands."
"9124","9097 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah: {And We guided him to the two paths}. He said: The path of good and evil."
"9125","9098 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sharik narrated, from al-Suddi, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that he was asked about al-suht? He said: Bribes. It was said: In judgment? He said: That is disbelief."
"9126","9099 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: Al-suht is bribery in religion."
"9127","9100 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Hammad ibn Yahya al-Abahh narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, he said: Bribery in judgment is disbelief, and among the people it is suht."
"9128","9101 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Israil narrated, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Masruq, he said: I asked Ibn Masud about bribery in judgment? He said: That is disbelief."
"9129","9102 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Suddi, from Murrah, from Abdullah, they said: {Our Lord, whoever brought this upon us, increase him double punishment in the Fire}. He said: Vipers and snakes."
"9130","9103 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {We increased them punishment above punishment}. He said: They were given more scorpions, whose fangs are like tall palm trees."
"9131","9104 - Abu Yazid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Yahya ibn Isa narrated, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning His saying: {We increased them punishment above punishment}. He said: Scorpions whose fangs are like tall palm trees."
"9132","9105 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah or Muslim - Sufyan doubted - from Masruq, from Abdullah, the like of it."
"9133","9106 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Israil narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, concerning the saying of the Blessed and Exalted: {Then they shall meet ghayy}. He said: A valley in Jahannam."
"9134","9107 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, {Then they shall meet ghayy}. He said: A river in Jahannam."
"9135","9108 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father, he said: Al-ghayy is a river in Jahannam into which those who followed desires are cast."
"9136","9109 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, regarding {They will meet ghayy}: he said: A valley in Hell of pus."
"9137","9110 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, regarding {They will meet ghayy}: he said: A river in Hell and a valley in Hell."
"9138","9111 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Said ibn Amir al-Dubai narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, regarding His saying {They will meet ghayy}: he said: A valley in Hell, deep-bottomed, foul in food."
"9139","9112 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah: he said: It is a river in the Fire called Ghayy."
"9140","9113 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, regarding His saying {They will meet ghayy}: he said: A river in Hell called Ghayy."
"9141","9114 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sharik narrated, from al-Amash, from Dharr, from Wail ibn Mahanah, from Abdullah: he said: Wayl is a valley in Hell of pus."
"9142","9115 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, regarding {And let them not display their adornment except what is apparent thereof}: he said: The garments."
"9143","9116 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, regarding {And let them not display their adornment except what is apparent thereof}: he said: The adornment is the earring, the armlet, the anklet, and the necklace."
"9144","9117 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Hudayj ibn Muawiyah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, regarding His saying {And let them not display their adornment}: he said: The adornment is the bracelet, the armlet, the anklet, the ornament, the earring, and the necklace; and what is apparent is the garments and the cloak."
"9145","9118 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, regarding {They thrust their hands into their mouths}: he said: They bit them."
"9146","9119 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, regarding His saying {They thrust their hands into their mouths}: he said: They bit their fingers in rage."
"9147","9120 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Waki narrated, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, regarding His saying {There is none of you but will come to it}: he said: The bridge."
"9148","9121 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Said ibn Amir narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, regarding His saying {The Fire will scorch their faces while they grimace therein}: he said: Have you not looked at heads burnt crisp, their teeth exposed and their lips shrunk."
"9149","9122 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Yazid ibn Ata narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Masud, that he was asked about this verse {They will have collars of what they withheld tied around them on the Day of Resurrection}: he said: He will be collared with a bald serpent pecking at his head."
"9150","9123 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah: he said: Whoever had wealth and did not pay its zakat will be collared on the Day of Resurrection with a bald serpent pecking at his head, saying: I am your wealth which you used to withhold. {They will have collars of what they withheld tied around them on the Day of Resurrection}."
"9151","9124 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, regarding {They will have collars of what they withheld tied around them on the Day of Resurrection}: he said: His wealth will come as a snake pecking at his head, saying: I am your wealth which you withheld, and he will be collared with it."
"9152","9125 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, regarding the saying of Allah Almighty {They will have collars of what they withheld tied around them on the Day of Resurrection}: he said: He will be collared with a bald serpent with two spots on its mouth pecking at his head, saying: What is between me and you; and it will say: I am your wealth which you withheld."
"9153","9126 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Israil narrated, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Masruq: he said: We asked Abdullah ibn Masud about His saying {They will have collars of what they withheld tied around them on the Day of Resurrection}: he said: A serpent biting his jaw."
"9154","9127 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar: he said: I heard Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud saying: Abdullah ibn Masud used to pray Maghrib when the eyebrow of the sun set, then he would swear that it is the time about which Allah Almighty said {Establish prayer at the decline of the sun}."
"9155","9128 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah: he said: The decline of the sun is its setting; the Arabs say: when the sun sets, when the sun declines, openly."
"9156","9129 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah: he said: Its decline is its setting."
"9157","9130 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Masud: he said: The decline of the sun is its setting."
"9158","9131 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: he said: Abdullah prayed Maghrib, and when he finished we kept glancing, and he said: Why are you glancing? We said: We think the sun is still up. He said: This, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is the appointed time of this prayer. Then he recited: {Establish prayer at the decline of the sun to the darkness of the night}; so this is the decline of the sun, and this is the darkness of the night."
"9159","9132 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: he said: Abdullah prayed one day while a man kept watching whether the sun had set, so Abdullah said: What are you looking at? This, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is the appointed time of this prayer. Allah Almighty says: {Establish prayer at the decline of the sun to the darkness of the night}; so this is the decline of the sun, and this is the darkness of the night."
"9160","9133 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Hushaym narrated, from al-Shaybani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: he said: We were with Abdullah when he gave salam, and he said: This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is when the sun has declined, and the time of this prayer has begun."
"9161","9134 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: he said: We were with Abdullah ibn Masud, and when the sun set he said: This, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is when the sun has declined, and the time of prayer has begun."
"9162","9135 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah: he said: The decline of the sun is its setting."
"9163","9136 - Al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah: he said: The decline of the sun is when it disappears."
"9164","9137 - Al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah: he said: Its setting."
"9165","9138 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Waki narrated, from Misar, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, the like of it."
"9166","9139 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah: he said: Abdullah used to say: The two watches of angels of Allah overtake one another, the night watch and the day watch, at the rising of dawn; and recite if you wish: {And the recitation of dawn; indeed the recitation of dawn is witnessed}."
"9167","9140 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sharik narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: he said: We were with Abdullah on the road to Makkah, and when the sun set he said: This is the darkness of the night. Then the call to prayer was made, then he said: This, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is the time of this prayer."
"9168","9141 - Al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah, regarding {To the darkness of the night}: he said: The last Isha."
"9169","9142 - Al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Jabir, from Amir, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah: he said: The last Isha."
"9170","9143 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abdullah ibn al-Mukhariq, from his father al-Mukhariq ibn Sulaym, from Abdullah, regarding {Then he will have a constricted life}: he said: The punishment of the grave."
"9171","9144 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abdullah ibn al-Mukhariq, from his father Mukhariq ibn Sulaym: that Abdullah used to say: When I narrate a hadith to you, I bring you confirmation of it from the Book of Allah. When the Muslim servant says: Praise be to Allah, Glory be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, and Blessed is Allah, an angel takes them and places them under his wing, then ascends with them; he does not pass any company of angels but they seek forgiveness for the one who said them, until he brings them to the Face of the Merciful, Exalted. Then Abdullah recited: {To Him ascend the good words, and righteous deeds raise them}."
"9172","9145 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abdullah ibn Mukhariq ibn Sulaym, from his father: Abdullah said: When I narrate a hadith to you, I inform you of its confirmation. When the Muslim servant dies, he is sat up in his grave and it is said to him: Who is your Lord? What is your religion? Who is your Prophet? So Allah makes him firm and he says: My Lord is Allah, my religion is Islam, and my Prophet is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then his grave is widened for him and opened up for him. Then Abdullah recited: {Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter, and Allah leaves the wrongdoers astray}."
"9173","9146 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abdullah ibn al-Mukhariq, from his father: Abdullah ibn Masud said: When we narrate a hadith to you, we bring you its confirmation from the Book of Allah: The drop stays in the womb forty, then it becomes a clot forty, then it becomes a lump forty; then when Allah Almighty wants to create the creation, an angel descends and Allah says to him: Write. He says: My Lord, what shall I write? He says: Write: wretched or fortunate, male or female, what is his provision, what is his trace, what is his term? So Allah Almighty reveals to him what He wills, and the angel writes. Then Abdullah recited: {Indeed We created man from a mingled drop to test him}. He said: And Abdullah said: The mingling is the veins."
"9174","9147 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Arfajah, from Abdullah, who recited this verse {But you prefer the life of this world}: and said: Do you know with what the life of this world began? For what did he prefer the life of this world? The world was hastened for us, we were given its pleasure and its splendor, the Hereafter was hidden from us and folded away from us, so we answered the immediate and left the deferred."
"9175","9148 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: he said: I saw Abdullah erasing the two Muawwidhas, saying: Why do you add what is not in it?"
"9176","9149 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu Umar Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated; and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated; both said: Shubah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah, that he used to erase the two Muawwidhas from his mushaf, saying: They should not have mixed into it what is not in it."
"9177","9150 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ishkab narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Man narrated, from his father, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, that he used to erase the two Muawwidhas from the mushaf, saying: They are not from the Book of Allah."
"9178","9151 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated, Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Hasan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ibn Masud, that he used to say: Do not mix into the Quran what is not in it; they are only two protective supplications with which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge: {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak} and {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind}; and Abdullah used to wipe them out of the mushaf."
"9179","9152 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated, from al-Salt ibn Bahram, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that he used to erase the two Muawwidhas from the masahif, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only commanded seeking refuge with them, and he did not recite them."
"9180","9153 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, al-Masudi narrated, Qays ibn Muslim narrated, from Tariq ibn Shihab, that a man met a man afflicted with scrofula, and he said: Were it not that a pledge was taken from me I would have told you; that reached Abdullah ibn Masud, so he met him and said: Tell. He said: A pledge was taken from me not to narrate it to anyone. Abdullah said to him: It should not have been taken from you; expiate your oath and narrate it. He said: Take the urine of camels of arak - meaning camels eating arak - cook it until it thickens, then drink it, and take arak leaves, crush them and sprinkle them on it. He said: He did so and was cured."
"9181","9154 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abu al-Umays narrated, from al-Qasim: he said: Abdullah said: The drinkers are in charge over the people above them."
"9182","9155 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah: he said: Guard your children in prayer, and accustom them to good, for good is habit."
"9183","9156 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah: he said: Accustom yourselves to good, for good is only by habit."
"9184","9157 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abu al-Umays narrated, from Imran ibn Umayr, from his father, that Abdullah freed a slave boy of his, saying: Your wealth is indeed mine, but I have left it for you."
"9185","9158 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shubah narrated, Yahya ibn Amr ibn Salamah informed me, from his father, that he heard Abdullah saying: For me to equip a whip in the path of Allah is dearer to me than a Hajj after the Hajj of Islam."
"9186","9159 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Israil informed me, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah: he said: The millstone of Islam will turn at the head of thirty-five, then a great event will occur; if their destruction is in it, then likely so; otherwise it will stretch over them seventy years; whoever lives to that will see what he disapproves. Thus Abu al-Ahwas narrated it as stopped; and Masruq, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, and al-Bara ibn Najiyah raised it."
"9187","9160 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Israil informed me, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah or Ibn Yazid, from Abdullah: he said: A man may utter a word making his companions laugh, gaining nothing from it for his family, descending with it farther than from heaven to earth."
"9188","9161 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abu Awn, from al-Qasim, that a man asked permission of his heirs to bequeath more than a third, and they permitted him, then they went back on it after he died; Abdullah was asked about that and said: That is the abomination; it is not allowed."
"9189","9162 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abu al-Umays narrated, from Abu Awn, from al-Qasim, from Abdullah, regarding a man who makes a bequest and the heirs approve it, then they go back: Abdullah said: That is the abomination; it is not allowed."
"9190","9163 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, al-Thawri informed me, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Ibn Masud: he said: Allah Almighty did not send down a disease but He sent down with it a cure; so take to cow's milk, for it grazes from all trees."
"9191","9164 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab: he said: Abdullah said: Allah did not send down a disease but He sent down for it a healing except old age; so take to cow's milk, for it grazes from all trees."
"9192","9165 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father: he said: Abdullah would not make qunut in any of the prayers except in witr before the rakah."
"9193","9166 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abu al-Umays narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to me, from his father: he said: Abdullah would not make qunut in the dawn prayer, and when he made qunut in witr he made it before the rakah."
"9194","9167 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from two men among the companions of Abdullah, that they used to draw their heads near Abdullah to hear what he said in his prostration: one of them said: I heard him saying: Glory be to You, there is no god besides You; and the other said: I heard him saying: Glory be to You, there is no Lord besides You."
"9195","9168 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Malik ibn Asma ibn Kharijah, from his father: he said: I heard Abdullah saying: The one with two tongues in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"9196","9169 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abu Ubaydah: he said: Abdullah said: Hasten to the Fridays, for Allah Almighty appears to the people of Paradise every Friday on a dune of camphor, and they will be in nearness according to their hastening to Friday; then Allah Almighty creates for them of honor something they had not seen before that, then they return to their families and tell them of what Allah created for them. He said: Then Abdullah entered the mosque and there were two men on Friday who had preceded him, so Abdullah said: Two men and I am the third; if Allah wills He will bless the third."
"9197","9170 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abu Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Babah: he said: Abdullah said: Let no Muslim man mock whatever state of the world he wakes or sleeps in, lest there be resentment in himself."
"9198","9171 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abu Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Babah: he said: Abdullah said: For one of you to bite on a coal until it cools, or hold onto it until it cools, is better than saying of a matter decreed by Allah: would that it had not been."
"9199","9172 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abu Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Babah: he said: Abdullah said: If I knew that only ten nights remained of my term, I would love that a woman not leave me during them."
"9200","9173 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abu al-Husayn meaning Ziyad ibn Fayyad, from Tamim ibn Salamah: he said: Abdullah said: The one who raises his head before the imam raises his head is not safe from his head turning into a dog's head; and people who raise their sights to the sky will stop, or their sights will be snatched away."
"9201","9174 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from Ziyad ibn Fayyad, from Tamim ibn Salamah: he said: Abdullah said: None of you is safe, raising his head in prayer before the imam, from his head turning into a dog's head; and people who raise their sights in prayer will stop, or it will not return to them."
"9202","9175 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, al-Thawri informed me, from Ziyad ibn Fayyad, from Tamim ibn Salamah: he said: Abdullah said: A man is not secure, when he raises his head before the imam, from his head turning into a dog's head; people who raise their sights to the sky will stop, or it will not return to them."
"9203","9176 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Sulayman ibn Mina, from Nufay mawla Abdullah: he said: Abdullah was among the people finest in white garment, and among the people sweetest in scent."
"9204","9177 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Humayd ibn Abdullah ibn al-Asamm narrated: he said: I heard Abu Qays al-Awdi: he said: Perfume pleased Abdullah."
"9205","9178 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Humayd ibn Abdullah ibn al-Asamm narrated, from Abu Qays: he said: Abdullah entered the mosque on Friday wearing pure fine white clothes, looked at a spacious place and sat, and did not step over anyone. He said: The imam came out, and two men were talking, so he took pebbles and threw at them; they looked at him and fell silent. When the imam came down he said: Did you not know that you are in prayer."
"9206","9179 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abu Husayn, from al-Qasim, from Masruq: he said: Abdullah disliked for the judge of the Muslims to take a stipend for it, and for the keeper of their spoils."
"9207","9180 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Dalham ibn Salih narrated, Humayd ibn Abdullah al-Thaqafi narrated to me: that Alqamah ibn Qays borrowed a thousand dirhams from Abdullah and he lent them to him; when the stipend came out he brought a thousand dirhams and said: This is your wealth. He said: Bring it. He took it, and Abdullah said to him: Were it not dislike of opposing you I would have kept the wealth. Abdullah said: We have more right to it. He sat talking a while, then stood and left; Alqamah went, and when he reached the people of the coffers Abdullah sent after him and brought him back, saying: Are you in need? He said: Yes. He said: Take the wealth. When he took it Abdullah said: For me to lend wealth twice is dearer to me than to give it in charity once."
"9208","9181 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Umar ibn Dharr narrated, Mujahid narrated to me, that Abdullah ibn Masud sent a sacrificial camel with a man, saying: What shall I do with it? He said: Eat you and your companions a third, send to our Bedouins a third, and give a third in charity."
"9209","9182 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Muti al-Ghazzal narrated, from al-Hakam, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah: he said: When one of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek the correct in himself, complete upon it, then prostrate two prostrations after the salam while sitting."
"9210","9183 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from al-Hakam, from Abu Wail: he said: Abdullah said: Whoever doubts or errs in his prayer, let him seek the correct then prostrate two prostrations."
"9211","9184 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated: he said: I heard Malik asking al-Shabi about the tashahhud? He said: Ibn Masud used to say after Peace be upon you O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah: Peace upon us from our Lord."
"9212","9185 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated: he said: I asked al-Hasan about nabidh? He said: I drink only in something tied shut. His son said: Did not Ibn Masud used to drink with you in the green jar? He said: Yes."
"9213","9186 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Uqbah ibn Wahb ibn Uqbah al-Amiri al-Bakkai narrated: he said: I heard my father Wahb ibn Uqbah narrating from Yazid ibn Muawiyah al-Amiri, that he heard Abdullah ibn Masud saying: How will you be when you see a people, or a people come to you, smeared faces?"
"9214","9187 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Uqbah ibn Wahb narrated, I heard my father narrating from Yazid ibn Muawiyah, that Abdullah ibn Masud went out to the market, and there was a man saying: People fighting in the market; I have never seen like today the misleading tribulation. He said: This is not the misleading tribulation, but this is a horn of Satan."
"9215","9188 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn Ata al-Amiri al-Bakkai narrated: he said: I heard Wahb ibn Uqbah narrating from Yazid ibn Muawiyah, from Ibn Masud, the like of it."
"9216","9189 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, from Abu Ishaq, Hubayrah ibn Yarim narrated to me, that he heard Ibn Masud saying: Among the last of the people of Paradise to enter is a man whom his Lord Almighty passes by and says to him: Stand and enter Paradise. He turns to Him frowning and says: Have You left anything for me? He says: Yes; for you is the like of what the sun rose or set upon."
"9217","9190 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami: he said: Abdullah ibn Masud prayed Fajr in one of the mosques of Banu Asad, and their imam led them with the two longest surahs of the Mufassal according to the arrangement of Abdullah; when he finished the prayer he said: Do I not see you, a young man, reciting these two surahs in this prayer while you are young."
"9218","9191 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim: he said: A man perfumed with embalming scent came to Abdullah, and when he saw him and smelled the embalming he said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from his evil. He said: He came and mentioned to him that he had fallen upon his wife's slave girl, so establish the hadd upon me. He said: Seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him, conceal yourself, and if you can free her, free her."
"9219","9192 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, that Abdullah used to say takbir when he finished recitation, then when he finished qunut he said takbir and bowed."
"9220","9193 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Layth, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Alqamah, that a man asked Abdullah about the time of Zuhr? He said: That a man steps with his shadow until the shadow of everything becomes like it; and he asked him about the time of Asr? He said: Pray it while the sun is white, alive; and asked about the time of Maghrib? He said: When the sun falls."
"9221","9194 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Layth, from al-Hakam: Abdullah ibn Masud said: I warm myself with it in winter, and cool myself with it in summer."
"9222","9195 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj: he said: I was informed that Ibn Masud used to warm himself with his wife in winter while he was junub, though he had bathed, and cool himself with her in summer while they were so."
"9223","9196 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Layth, from Wabarah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that a cousin of his swore abstention from his wife for ten days, then went out and came back after four months had passed, and had intercourse with his family; he met a man and reminded him of his oath, so he came to Ibn Masud and asked him; he made him swear by Allah that he did not know, then sent to his wife and made her swear by Allah Almighty that she did not know, then ordered him to propose to her for himself."
"9224","9197 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Layth, from al-Hakam and Talhah ibn Musarrif: both said: Maqil ibn Sinan came to Abdullah and asked him about a man who vowed a vow without naming anything? He said: He frees a slave."
"9225","9198 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from al-Qasim: he said: Abdullah was brought a slave girl who stole though she had not menstruated, and he did not cut her."
"9226","9199 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from al-Qasim: Abdullah said: Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills, has made exception."
"9227","9200 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from al-Qasim: he said: Abdullah bought from his wife - or from a wife of his - a slave girl and stipulated for her, and she stipulated her service; Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: There is nothing of your wealth in which there is a reservation for another."
"9228","9201 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim: he said: Abdullah said takbir when he opened the prayer, saying like this; and Misar raised his hands above his chest."
"9229","9202 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated: he said: I heard al-Ala al-Anbari mentioning from a man, that Abdullah stood in the two rakahs and did not sit."
"9230","9203 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, al-Thawri informed me, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Mustawrid ibn al-Ahnaf: he said: A man came to Ibn Masud saying: My uncle married me to his slave girl, she bore me children, and he wants to enslave them. He said: That is not for him."
"9231","9204 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Mustawrid: he said: A man came to Abdullah saying: His uncle married him to his slave girl, and he wants to enslave his child. He said: That is not for him."
"9232","9205 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah: he said: Abdullah kept saying talbiyah until he threw the jamrah."
"9233","9206 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from Abdullah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi, that he heard Abdullah saying while bowing: There is no power and no strength except with Allah."
"9234","9207 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from Man ibn Abd al-Rahman, from a man: he said: Abdullah said to a man: When you ask your Lord for good, do not ask while a stone is in your hand."
"9235","9208 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Misar narrated, from Abu Husayn: he said: Abdullah said: Rise in the morning oiled, fasting."
"9236","9209 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abu al-Umays narrated, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab: he said: A woman of us wanted Hajj and wanted to combine an Umrah with her Hajj, so she asked Abdullah; he said: I find this only the months of Hajj; Allah Almighty said: {Known months}."
"9237","9210 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud said: His saying returned to washing the feet in His saying {And your feet to the ankles}."
"9238","9211 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Miskin, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Masud: he said: A man must scrub between his fingers in wudu, or the Fire will scrub him."
"9239","9212 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Abu Miskin narrated, from Huzayl, from Abdullah: he said: A man must scrub between his fingers with purification, or the Fire will scrub him."
"9240","9213 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Mansur, from Talhah ibn Musarrif: he said: I was told of Abdullah ibn Masud that he said: Run water through the five fingers, lest Allah fill them with Fire."
"9241","9214 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar and al-Thawri and Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Arqam ibn Shurahbil: he said: I scratched my body while in prayer and reached my private part, so I mentioned it to Abdullah ibn Masud; he said to me: Cut it off - laughing - where would you put it away from you; it is only a piece of you."
"9242","9215 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abd al-Rahman, from Alqamah: he said: Abdullah ibn Masud was asked, while I was listening, about touching the private part; he said: Is it but like the tip of your nose?"
"9243","9216 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Jubayr, that Ibn Masud said: I do not care whether I touched it or my nose."
"9244","9217 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Masud, that he said: I do not care whether I touched it or my knee."
"9245","9218 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from five of the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Ali ibn Abi Talib, Ibn Masud, Hudhayfah, Imran ibn Husayn, and another man; some of them said: I do not care whether I touched my private part or my nose; and another said: My ear; and another said: My thigh; and another said: My knee."
"9246","9219 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar: he said: Ibn Masud prayed with dung and blood of a slaughtered camel on his belly, and did not perform wudu."
"9247","9220 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Ibn Sirin: he said: Ibn Masud slaughtered a camel and was stained with its blood and dung; prayer was established and he prayed without performing wudu."
"9248","9221 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna, Rabah ibn al-Harith narrated to me, that Ibn Masud said regarding carrion: Its tanning is its slaughter."
"9249","9222 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Ibn Masud: he said: For me to perform wudu from a foul word is dearer to me than to perform wudu from wholesome food."
"9250","9223 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Masud: he said: For me to perform wudu from a foul word is dearer to me than to perform wudu from a wholesome morsel."
"9251","9224 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abdullah: he said: My performing wudu from a foul word is dearer to me than performing wudu from wholesome food."
"9252","9225 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn al-Taymi, from Mansur, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, that Ali, Ibn Masud, and al-Shabi said regarding a man who sleeps while sitting: He has no wudu upon him."
"9253","9226 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ubaydah, that Ibn Masud said: A man performs wudu from direct contact, from touching with his hand, and from a kiss when he kisses his wife; and he used to say regarding this verse {Or you have touched women}: it is the pinch."
"9254","9227 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim: he said: I heard Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah saying: Abdullah ibn Masud said: The kiss is of touching, and from it is wudu."
"9255","9228 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Bayan, from al-Shabi, from Abdullah: he said: Touching is what is less than intercourse."
"9256","9229 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah ibn Masud: he said: Touching is what is less than intercourse, that a man touches his wife's body with desire; in it is wudu."
"9257","9230 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Hammad, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Masud: he said: Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and takes a hair of his backside, making him think he has broken wudu; let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."
"9258","9231 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Qays ibn al-Sakan: he said: Ibn Masud said: Satan hovers around a man in his prayer to cut off his prayer; when he fails, he blows in his backside; if one of you senses anything of that, let him not leave until he finds a smell or hears a sound."
"9259","9232 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Qays ibn al-Sakan, from Ibn Masud: he said: Satan hovers around a man in prayer to cut off his prayer; when he fails, he blows in his backside to show him that he has broken wudu; if he finds anything of that, let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."
"9260","9233 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim: he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: Satan blows in a man's backside; if one of you senses that, let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."
"9261","9234 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah: he said: A bowl was brought to us while we were with Ibn Masud, and he ordered it placed in the road; he ate from it and we ate, and he kept inviting whoever passed by; then we went to prayer, and he did no more than wash the tips of his fingers and rinse his mouth, then prayed."
"9262","9235 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah: he said: A bowl was brought to us from the house of Ibn Masud, containing bread and meat; we ate, with Ibn Masud among us; then he rinsed and washed his fingers at Maghrib."
"9263","9236 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah: he said: A bowl was brought to us; we ate with Abdullah among us; then Abdullah rinsed and washed his fingers, then we went to Maghrib prayer."
"9264","9237 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Wail ibn Dawud, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah ibn Masud: he said: Wudu is only from what exits, not from what enters; and fasting is from what enters, not from what exits."
"9265","9238 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abd al-Ala, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, my mother narrated to me, that Abdullah used to wear his khuffs at Fajr prayer, then not remove them until he went to his bed."
"9266","9239 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Masud, that he used to wipe over socks and sandals."
"9267","9240 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd: he said: Abdullah set wiping as three days for the traveler and a day for the resident."
"9268","9241 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq: he said: I traveled with Abdullah ibn Masud three days to Madinah and he did not remove his khuffs."
"9269","9242 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq: he said: I traveled with Abdullah to Madinah and he did not remove his khuffs for three days and their nights. Sulayman said: I narrated this hadith of Shaqiq to Ibrahim, and he said: And Abu Ubaydah narrated to me from Amr ibn al-Harith this hadith."
"9270","9243 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq: he said: I traveled with Abdullah ibn Masud and he used to wipe over his khuffs three days."
"9271","9244 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Amir, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Masud: he said: For the traveler three days wiping over khuffs, and for the resident a day and a night; and I traveled with Abdullah and he stayed three days wiping over khuffs."
"9272","9245 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ali, from Abdullah ibn Masud: he said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"9273","9246 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated, Hammad narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abdullah ibn Masud: he said: The traveler wipes over khuffs three days and their nights, and the resident a day and a night."
"9274","9247 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud: he said: The traveler wipes three days and their nights, and the resident a day and a night."
"9275","9248 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Aban informed me, from al-Nakhai, from Alqamah, that a man had smallpox; so Ibn Masud ordered dust brought in a basin - or a vessel - and he wiped with dust."
"9276","9249 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Araj, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Masud: he said: If I became junub then did not find water for a month, I would not pray. Sufyan said: It is not acted upon."
"9277","9250 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Abu Sinan, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, that Ibn Masud abandoned his saying about the junub that he does not wash."
"9278","9251 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi: he said: al-Harith narrated to me from Ali, and Alqamah from Abdullah ibn Masud, and Masruq from Aishah: they said: When circumcision passes circumcision, ghusl becomes obligatory. Masruq said: And she was the most knowledgeable of them about that."
"9279","9252 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, that Ibn Masud was asked about that? He said: When you reach that, you wash. Sufyan said: And the community is upon ghusl."
"9280","9253 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim: he said: Abdullah was asked about a man who has intercourse with his wife but does not ejaculate? He said: As for me, when I reach that of a woman, I wash."
"9281","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, who said: al-Harith ibn al-Azma informed me, who said: I heard Abdullah saying: Any person in major ritual impurity who washes with khitmi (marshmallow plant) has done sufficiently."
"9282","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn al-Azma, from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: If he washes his head while in major impurity with khitmi, he has done sufficiently, and it does not harm him if he does not pour water over it."
"9283","Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn al-Azma, from Abdullah, who said: When one of you washes his head while junub with khitmi, then performs ghusl afterwards, let him wash his head with water if he wishes."
"9284","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn al-Azma, that Ibn Masud used to wash his head with khitmi while junub, then perform ghusl, and not wash his head again."
"9285","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, who said: When a junub person washes his head with khitmi, that suffices him instead of washing it with water."
"9286","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from a man from Tayyi, from his father, that Ibn Masud went out to the mosque and began to trot, so it was said to him: Do you do this while you forbid it? He said: I only hastened; the mark of the prayer is the first takbir."
"9287","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Layth, from a man from Tayyi, from his father, who said: I met Abdullah ibn Masud coming out of his house trotting, so I trotted with him, and I said: You have done something you used to forbid us. He said: I hastened to catch the prayer."
"9288","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, that Abu Musa al-Ashari led them and removed his sandals, so Abdullah said to him: Why did you remove your sandals? Are you in the sacred valley?"
"9289","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Alqamah, though he did not hear it from him, that Abdullah ibn Masud visited Abu Musa al-Ashari in his house and the prayer came; Abu Musa said to him: Come forward, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, for you are older and more knowledgeable. He said: No, rather you come forward, for we came to you in your house and your mosque. So Abu Musa came forward and removed his sandals; when he had prayed, he (Abdullah) said: What did you intend by removing them? Are you in the sacred valley Tuwa? I indeed saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in leather socks and sandals."
"9290","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Abu Ubaydah, who said: Ibn Masud would not pray - or he said - nor prostrate except on the ground."
"9291","Al-Thawri said: And Muhammad informed me, from Ibrahim, that he used to stand on bardi and prostrate on the ground. We said: What is bardi? He said: A mat."
"9292","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Wail, that Ibn Masud prayed on a mish (a coarse hair garment)."
"9293","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, who said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani saying: Ibn Masud used to patrol the mosque at night, and he would not leave any dark figure in it except he expelled him, except a man praying."
"9294","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: We were with Abdullah ibn Masud, and he wanted to spit, and there was no empty space on his right, so he disliked spitting on his right, though he was not in prayer."
"9295","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Asim, from Ibn Sirin or someone else, who said: Ibn Masud heard a man announcing a lost item in the mosque, so he silenced him and rebuked him and said: We have been forbidden from this."
"9296","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Qabisah ibn Burmah al-Asadi, from Ibn Masud, who said: I do not like your muezzins to be your blind men - he said, and I think he said - nor your reciters."
"9297","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Wasil, from Qabisah ibn Burmah, from Ibn Masud, the same."
"9298","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: The entry into inviolability of prayer is the takbir, and its exit is the taslim; when you give salam and a need hastens you, then go before he turns his face toward you."
"9299","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, that he prayed with his companions in his house without iqamah, and said: The iqamah of the townspeople suffices."
"9300","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Ibn Masud, Alqamah, and al-Aswad prayed without adhan or iqamah. Sufyan said: The iqamah of the town sufficed them."
"9301","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud saw a man raising his hands to the sky supplicating while in his prayer, so Abdullah ibn Masud said: Little does he know; perhaps his sight will be snatched before it returns to him."
"9302","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam, from Ibn Masud, who said: When the prayer has been commenced, do not leave it for something else."
"9303","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Masud said to his companions: I do not spare you any effort regarding the time; then he led them in Zuhr, I think he said, when the sun had declined."
"9304","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, who said: Abdullah prayed when the sun had declined, so I said to Sulayman: Zuhr? He said: Yes. Then Abdullah said: This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the appointed time of this prayer."
"9305","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khishf ibn Malik, who said: Abdullah used to pray Zuhr while the grasshoppers were hopping from the heat of the scorching ground."
"9306","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Ibn Masud used to delay Asr."
"9307","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, who said: The sun rises between the two horns of Satan, and it does not rise the length of a spear except a gate of the gates of Hell is opened for it; when midday comes, the gates of Hell are opened for it. He said: So Abdullah used to forbid us two prayers at these two times: when it rises until it ascends, and at midday."
"9308","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud used to pray the morning prayer at spreading light (isfaar)."
"9309","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, who said: Abdullah used to say: Be brief in prayer, for behind you are the old, the weak, and the one with a need. We used to pray with our imam while wearing our garments, and he would recite a surah from the Miin (the long surahs), then we would go to Abdullah and find him still in prayer."
"9310","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, that he heard the son of Abdullah ibn Masud saying: Abdullah ibn Masud used to pray Fajr in darkness just as Ibn al-Zubayr prays it in darkness, and he used to pray Maghrib when the sun sets, and he would say: By Allah, it is indeed as Allah the Exalted said: {until the darkness of the night, and the recitation of dawn; indeed the recitation of dawn is witnessed}."
"9311","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, one who saw Ibn Masud narrated to me: He prayed Fajr, then sat and did not rise for any prayer until the call for Zuhr was made, then he rose and prayed four."
"9312","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Layth, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, who said: None of you should pray with an open gap between him and the qiblah - meaning an empty space."
"9313","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Layth, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, who said: Do not pray with a gap between you and the qiblah."
"9314","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from al-Aswad, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever among you is able not to let anyone pass in front of him while he prays, let him do so; for the one passing in front of the praying person is lesser in reward than the one passed in front of."
"9315","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, who said: If one of you is able that no one passes in front of him, let him do so; for the one passing over the praying person is lesser in reward than the one passed in front of."
"9316","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: Whoever among you is able not to let anyone pass in front of him while he prays, let him do so; for the one passing in front of the praying person is lesser than the one passed in front of."
"9317","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from a man from the people of Madinah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: When someone wants to pass in front of you while you pray, do not let him; for he takes away half your prayer."
"9318","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud used to level the pebbles with his hand once when he wanted to prostrate, and he would say in his prostration: Labbayk wa sadayk (At Your service, and at Your aid)."
"9319","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar or Umar ibn Rashid, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from a man, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who advance the rows with their prayer - meaning the foremost row."
"9320","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Madi Karib, who said: Ibn Masud said: Do not line up between the pillars, and do not follow in prayer people who are talking."
"9321","Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Madi Karib, who said: Abdullah said: Do not follow in prayer people who argue, and do not pray between the pillars."
"9322","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri and Ibn Uyaynah, from Abu Ishaq, from Madi Karib al-Hamdani, who said: I heard Ibn Masud saying: Do not line up between the columns, and do not pray with people passing in front of you."
"9323","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl al-Nakhai narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Madi Karib, from Abdullah, who said: I disliked prayer only between the columns, one or two."
"9324","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, that Ibn Masud used to say takbir whenever he lowered and raised."
"9325","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Husayn, from Ibrahim, that Ibn Masud used to raise his hands at the first, then not raise afterwards."
"9326","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah would not raise his hands in any part of the prayer except the first takbir."
"9327","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that when he entered the prayer he raised his hands, then did not raise after that."
"9328","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, one whom I trust narrated to me, from Abu Bakr, from Umar, and from Uthman, and from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with them, that when they commenced they would say before recitation: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god besides You."
"9329","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ibn Masud, that he used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his arrogance, and his poetry."
"9330","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, who said: His hamz - meaning Satan's - is al-mutah, meaning madness; his blowing is pride; his spittle is poetry."
"9331","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Sad al-Baqqal, from Abu Wail, who said: Ali and Ibn Masud would not recite aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, nor the seeking of refuge, nor Amin."
"9332","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Uthman ibn Matar, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Asim, from Abu Wail, that Ibn Masud used to open his prayer with: {All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds}."
"9333","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, that Ibn Masud used to recite in Zuhr and Asr, in the first two rakahs, the Fatihat al-Kitab and a surah in each rakah, and in the last two the Fatihat al-Kitab."
"9334","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Ibn Masud led them in Isha and recited forty verses of al-Anfal, then recited in the second a surah from the Mufassal."
"9335","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Ibn Masud led us in Isha prayer; he began Surah al-Anfal until he reached: {What an excellent Protector and excellent Helper}, then bowed, then recited in the second rakah two surahs from the Mufassal."
"9336","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, who said: Abu Ishaq was asked: Did you mention, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Abdullah recited in the last Isha, in the first rakah: {They ask you about the spoils} until he reached: {What an excellent Protector and excellent Helper}, then bowed, then recited in the second a surah from the Mufassal? He said: Yes."
"9337","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud led us in the last Isha prayer; he began al-Anfal and recited until he reached: {What an excellent Protector and excellent Helper}, then bowed, then stood and recited in the second rakah a surah."
"9338","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, who said: A man came to Abdullah and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, shall I recite behind the imam? He said: Listen attentively to the Quran, for in prayer there is occupation, and the imam will suffice you that."
"9339","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Masud, that he said: Do not recite behind the imam unless he is an imam who does not recite."
"9340","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Ibn Masud would not recite behind the imam, and Ibrahim adopted that. When Ibn Masud was imam he recited in the first two rakahs, and would not recite anything in the last two."
"9341","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Masud, who said: When the imam falters, do not prompt him, for that is speech."
"9342","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Ibn Masud disliked prompting the imam, and said: It is speech."
"9343","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, who said: We prayed with Abdullah; when he bowed he joined his palms and placed them between his knees, and he struck our hands, so we did that."
"9344","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, that Ibn Masud bowed and joined his hands and placed them between his knees."
"9345","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah used to join his hands when he bowed, placing his hands between his knees and spreading his forearms over his thighs."
"9346","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, that Abdullah used to say in his bowing: My Lord, forgive me."
"9347","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Shaqiq, who said: Abdullah would often say in his bowing and prostration: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; there is no god besides You."
"9348","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu al-Aswad and Shaddad ibn al-Azma, from Ibn Masud - he said: They differed, so Abu al-Aswad said: Abdullah used to say in his prostration: Glory be to You, there is no Lord besides You. Shaddad said: He used to say: Glory be to You, there is no god besides You."
"9349","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from Shuayb, his uncle, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah, who said: I entered the mosque and found Abdullah praying; he bowed, and I began Surah al-Araf and finished it before he prostrated."
"9350","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: When the imam says: Allah hears the one who praises Him, let those behind him say: Our Lord, to You belongs praise."
"9351","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: When the imam says: Allah hears the one who praises Him, let those behind him say: Our Lord, to You belongs praise."
"9352","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, who said: Abdullah said: When one of you prostrates, let him not prostrate twisted nor lying down; when he performs prostration well, all his bones prostrate."
"9353","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, who said: When one of you prostrates, let him not prostrate lying down nor twisted; when he performs prostration well, every limb of him prostrates."
"9354","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid saying: I watched Abdullah ibn Masud in prayer and saw him rise without sitting. He said: He rises on the front of his feet in the first and second rakah."
"9355","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah would rise on the front of his feet."
"9356","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid narrated to me, that Ibn Masud would rise on the front of his feet; I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid narrated to me that Ibn Masud used to do it."
"9357","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to me, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah, when he said takbir as he raised his head from prostration, would stand up with it."
"9358","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar and al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud passed a man prostrating with his head tied up, so he undid it; when he finished, Abdullah said to him: Do not tie it up, for your hair prostrates, and for every hair you have reward. He said: I tied it only so it would not get dusty. He said: Its getting dusty is better for you."
"9359","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Zayd, who said: Abdullah passed a man prostrating who had tied up his head, so he undid his knot and released it, then waited until he prayed; then Abdullah said: Your hair prostrates with you, so do not tie it up, for for every hair of it you have reward. The man said: I feared it would get dusty. Abdullah said: Its getting dusty is better for you."
"9360","Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah, the same."
"9361","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, who said: Abdullah would not turn around in prayer; if his need was on his right, he left to the right, and if his need was on his left, he left to the left."
"9362","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar and al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, that he used to say: When the imam gives salam, leave toward wherever your need is, right or left, and do not turn around like the turning of a donkey."
"9363","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, who said: When Ibn Masud's need was on his left, he left to the left, and when his need was on his right, he left to the right."
"9364","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: When the imam gives salam, let him stand or move away from his place. I said: Does moving from his place and facing the qiblah suffice him? He said: Moving aside is going east or west - from more than one authority."
"9365","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, that when he gave salam he would stand from his place or move eastward or westward."
"9366","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: When the imam gives salam and a man has a need, let him not wait for him, when he gives salam, to face him with his face; the conclusion of prayer is the taslim. Abdullah, when he gave salam, would soon stand or move from his place and face them with his face."
"9367","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, that Ibn Masud said: When you are behind the imam, do not bow until he bows, do not prostrate until he prostrates, and do not raise your head before him; when the imam finishes and does not stand or move, and you have a need, then go and leave him, for your prayer is complete."
"9368","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abu Khalid - from the companions of Abdullah - who said: A man came to Abdullah and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, so-and-so recites the Quran while bowing and while prostrating. Abdullah said: There are men who recite the Quran and it does not pass their collarbones; when it enters the heart and becomes firmly rooted therein, it benefits."
"9369","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, who said: When Abdullah prayed, he was as if a garment thrown down."
"9370","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, who said: Keep the prayer settled. Mansur was asked: What does he mean by that? He said: Let him be settled in his prayer when he bows and when he prostrates."
"9371","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: Keep calm in prayer - meaning: Be still, be tranquil."
"9372","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Masud, who said: Allah continues to turn to the servant with His face so long as he does not turn away or break his ablution."
"9373","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from a man, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abu Ubaydah, who said: Ibn Masud passed a man standing with his feet together, and said: As for this one, he has missed the Sunnah; had he shifted between them it would be dearer to me."
"9374","Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Maysarah ibn Habib, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, the same."
"9375","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basriyyan narrated to us, both saying: Umar ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Maysarah ibn Habib, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, similar."
"9376","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, who said: Whoever catches the rakah has caught the prayer."
"9377","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, who said: Whoever catches the rakah has caught it."
"9378","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, that Hubayrah ibn Yarim informed him, from Ali and Ibn Masud, who said: Whoever does not catch the rakah should not count the prostration."
"9379","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ibn Masud, who said: Whoever misses the bowing should not count the prostration."
"9380","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: I and Abdullah entered the mosque with the people bowing; we bowed, then walked until we joined the people; they raised their heads and we raised with them; when we finished the prayer I stood to make it up, so Abdullah spoke to me and said: You have completed the prayer."
"9381","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: I and Ibn Masud entered the mosque with the imam bowing; we bowed, then moved until we were level with the row; when the imam finished I stood to make it up, so he said: You have caught it."
"9382","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: I entered the mosque with Ibn Masud with the people bowing; he bowed and I bowed with him, and we walked bowing until we reached the row; they raised their heads and we prayed our prayer; when the imam gave salam I thought I had missed it, so I stood to make it up; Ibn Masud pulled me and said: You have caught it."
"9383","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud said: There is no harm in bowing before the row."
"9384","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Nakhai, from Zayd ibn Ahmar, from Ibn Masud, who said: If one of you bows and walks to the row before they raise their heads, then he counts it; if they raise their heads before he reaches the row, he does not count it."
"9385","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud caught people sitting at the end of their prayer, and said: You have caught it, if Allah wills."
"9386","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah entered the mosque, and one with him entered; the imam bowed, so we bowed before we reached the row, then we reached the row when the imam said: Allah hears the one who praises Him; when the imam gave salam, Abdullah's companion stood to make it up, so Abdullah took his garment and said: Sit; you have caught the prayer."
"9387","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, that Ibn Masud hurried to prayer and was spoken to about it, so he said: Is prayer not the most rightful thing to hasten to?"
"9388","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Masud, who said: When a man doubts in his prayer, not knowing whether he prayed three or two, let him build on the most certain of that, then prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"9389","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Ibrahim, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Ibn Masud, that he said: He seeks the most correct of that, and prostrates the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"9390","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Aswad and Alqamah and the companions of Abdullah, that Abdullah used to say regarding forgetfulness: He seeks what is correct, and prostrates two prostrations while sitting after the taslim."
"9391","Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Khusayf, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Masud, who said: Forgetfulness is when he stands where one sits, or sits where one stands, or gives salam in two rakahs; he completes his prayer and prostrates two prostrations while sitting, reciting tashahhud in them."
"9392","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khusayf, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: If you stand or sit or give salam wrongly, prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then recite tashahhud, then give salam."
"9393","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah or someone else: Ibn Masud saw two men praying, one letting his lower garment hang and the other not completing his bowing or prostration, so he laughed. They said: What makes you laugh, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: I am amazed at these two men; as for the one letting his garment hang, Allah does not look at him, and as for the other, Allah does not accept his prayer."
"9394","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hammad informed us, from Ibrahim, who said: While Ibn Masud was sitting with his companions in the mosque, two men entered and stood behind two pillars; one prayed having let his garment hang, and the other did not complete his bowing or prostration; Ibn Masud kept looking at them, so his companions said: These two have distracted you from us. He said: Yes; as for this one, Allah does not look at him - meaning the one letting his garment hang - and as for this one, Allah does not accept from him - meaning the one who does not complete his bowing or prostration."
"9395","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Ibn Masud, that he saw a Bedouin praying who had let his garment hang, so he said: One who lets his garment hang in prayer has no standing before Allah, Mighty and Majestic, neither lawful nor unlawful."
"9396","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Masud, regarding a man who misses part of the prayer with the imam, who said: He makes what he catches with the imam the end of his prayer."
"9397","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, that Jundub and Masruq caught a rakah of Maghrib; Jundub recited and Masruq did not recite behind the imam; when the imam gave salam they stood to make up; Masruq sat in the second and third, and Jundub stood in the second and did not sit; when they finished they discussed that, then came to Ibn Masud, who said: Each was correct - or he said: Each did well - and we do as Masruq did."
"9398","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Jafar al-Jazari, from al-Hakam, that Jundub and Masruq caught a rakah of Maghrib; one of them recited in the last two rakahs what he had missed of recitation, and the other did not recite in one rakah; Ibn Masud was asked, and said: Both did well, and I do as the one did who recited in the two rakahs."
"9399","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Jundub and Masruq caught a rakah of the Maghrib prayer; when the imam gave salam they stood to make up; Jundub stood in the second rakah, and Masruq sat in both of them; they spoke to Ibn Masud about it, and he said: Both of you did well, and I do as Masruq did."
"9400","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, who said: Jundub and Masruq prayed Maghrib in a mosque, catching only a rakah with the imam; they stood to make up; Masruq sat in the second, and Jundub stood in the first rakah of the make-up; they came to Abdullah and mentioned that to him, and he said: Both of you did well, and do as Masruq did."
"9401","Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Ibrahim, that Masruq and Jundub reached the imam having missed a rakah; Masruq did not recite and Jundub recited; they mentioned that to Abdullah, who said: Both of you did not fall short of the matter, and the right word is what Masruq did."
"9402","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud said: Prayer has a fixed time like the time of Hajj."
"9403","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: Straighten your rows, for Satan slips through them like khadhf pebbles - or like the young of khadhf."
"9404","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, who said: One should not bow before the imam, nor rise before him, nor prostrate before him, nor rise before him."
"9405","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: The imam is appointed only to be followed; when he bows, bow, and when he rises, rise; do not precede him when he bows, when he rises, or when he prostrates; if your concern is only to catch up what he preceded you in, he prostrates before you and rises before you, so you catch that up."
"9406","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from an elder from Tayyi, who said: Ibn Masud passed one of our mosques; a man from them came forward and recited the Fatihat al-Kitab, then said: We perform Hajj to our Lord's House, and pay the debt, while it is like qata birds descending. Abdullah said: We never heard of this in the former religion; this is nothing but fabrication. Then Abdullah left."
"9407","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Alqamah and al-Aswad came with Ibn Masud to the mosque; the people met them having already prayed, so he took them back to the house, placed one of them on his right and the other on his left, then led them in prayer."
"9408","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, that Abdullah led Alqamah and al-Aswad in prayer; this one stood on his right and this one on his left, then he stood between them."
"9409","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Shabi, from Alqamah, that Ibn Masud led him and al-Aswad in prayer and stood between them."
"9410","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, the same."
"9411","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: When they are three, let them all line up together; when they are more than that, let one of them go ahead of them."
"9412","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Musa, who said: Ibn Masud came while the imam was praying Fajr, so he prayed two rakahs by a pillar, not having prayed the two rakahs of Fajr."
"9413","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Musa, from Ibn Masud, the same."
"9414","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Musa, from his father, who said: The prayer was established, so Abdullah went toward the mosque and prayed two rakahs, then entered the mosque."
"9415","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, that Ibn Masud used to say: Attach your needs to the prescribed prayer."
"9416","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from Abdullah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi, who said: I heard Abdullah's recitation in one of the two daytime prayers."
"9417","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, who said: I prayed beside Abdullah, and I did not know he was reciting anything until I heard him saying: {My Lord, increase me in knowledge}, so I knew he was in Ta-Ha."
"9418","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Husayn, from al-Haytham ibn Shihab, who said: I heard Ibn Masud saying: For one of you to sit on two hot stones is better for him than to sit cross-legged in prayer."
"9419","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Haytham ibn Shihab, who said: Abdullah said: For a man to sit on two hot stones is better for him than to sit cross-legged in prayer. Abd al-Razzaq said: That is, if he prayed standing, he should not sit cross-legged for the tashahhud, and if he prayed sitting, let him sit cross-legged."
"9420","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, that he said regarding a sick person praying: If he cannot reach the ground, let him gesture, and let him make his prostration lower than his bowing."
"9421","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Muawiyah, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, that Ibn Masud visited Utbah, his brother, while he was praying toward a siwak he raised to his face; he took it and threw it, then said: Gesture, and let your bowing place be higher than your prostration place."
"9422","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: Alqamah and al-Aswad visited Abdullah and said: The mother of al-Aswad is confined to sitting, and he fixes for her a fan-handle stick to pray toward; what do you think? He said: I see Satan presenting himself with the stick; let her prostrate on the ground if she can, otherwise let her gesture."
"9423","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, who said: I said to Alqamah: How was Abdullah's recitation? He said: The people of the house could hear his voice."
"9424","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Ibn Masud, who said: One who makes himself heard has not recited softly."
"9425","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: One who lets his ears hear has not recited softly."
"9426","9399 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sharik, Abu al-Ahwas, Yala ibn al-Harith and Abu Awanah narrated, from Ashath, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Abdullah, the same."
"9427","9400 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from al-Amash and al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Abdullah, the same."
"9428","9401 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: We asked Alqamah: How was the recitation of Abdullah at night? And he used to spend the night with him. He said: He used to let the household of his brother Utbah hear, while they were in a chamber before him."
"9429","9402 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: Alqamah used to spend the night with Abdullah, so we asked him: How did Abdullah recite? He said: He used to let the household of Utbah hear, while they were in a chamber before him."
"9430","9403 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I asked him, and he used to spend the night with Abdullah ibn Masud: When would Abdullah pray the witr? He said: He would pray the witr when there remained of the night like what had passed of the night at the time of the Maghrib prayer."
"9431","9404 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from Alqamah ibn Qays, he said: I spent a night with Abdullah ibn Masud. He stood at the beginning of the night, then he stood praying. He would recite the recitation of the imam in the mosque of his quarter, with tartil and without tarji, letting those around him hear, without raising his voice, until there did not remain of the darkness except like what is between the adhan for Maghrib and leaving it. Then he prayed the witr."
"9432","9405 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, Alqamah narrated to us, that Abdullah would pray the witr when there remained of the night about what had passed up to the Maghrib prayer."
"9433","9406 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Abdullah, he said: The witr is between the two prayers."
"9434","9407 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha and Abu Husayn, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, he said: Abdullah said: The witr is between the two prayers."
"9435","9408 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sharik narrated, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, Abu Husayn and Ayyash al-Amiri, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, he said: Abdullah said: The witr is between the two prayers: the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer."
"9436","9409 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Abu Husayn al-Asadi narrated, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: What is between the two prayers is witr: what is between the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer."
"9437","9410 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Abdullah, the same."
"9438","9411 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, that Ibn Masud said: The witr is between the two prayers."
"9439","9412 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, he said: I bear witness that I heard Abdullah ibn Masud calling out with it: The witr is between the two prayers: the last Isha prayer which you call atamah, and the Fajr prayer. Whenever you pray the witr, it is good."
"9440","9413 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Ibn Masud would pray the witr after the Fajr, and my father would pray the witr before the Fajr."
"9441","9414 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Ibn Masud, he said: I would not care if the Fajr prayer is established while I am praying the witr."
"9442","9415 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Masud, that he said: I do not care if the call for the Fajr prayer is made while I am in my wird and have not yet prayed the witr."
"9443","9416 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Qasim ibn Man narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Abu Maysarah, he said: A man came to Abdullah and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, is there witr after the adhan? He said: Yes, and after the iqamah."
"9444","9417 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, that Abdullah would pray the witr with three and more."
"9445","9418 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: Abdullah would pray the witr with three and more."
"9446","9419 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Ibn Masud said: The witr of the night is like the witr of the day: the Maghrib prayer, three."
"9447","9420 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: The witr is three, like the witr of the day: the Maghrib prayer."
"9448","9421 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Ibn Masud, he said: The witr is three rakahs like the Maghrib prayer."
"9449","9422 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Qasim ibn Man narrated, from Husayn, he said: It reached Ibn Masud that Sad prays the witr with one rakah. He said: One rakah never sufficed."
"9450","9423 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said to Sad ibn Abi Waqqas: Do you pray the witr with one? Sad said: Is the witr not one? Abdullah said: Yes, but three is better. Sad said: I will not add to it. So Abdullah became angry. Sad said: Do you get angry with me for praying the witr with one rakah, while you give inheritance to three grandmothers, yet you do not give inheritance to Hawwa, the wife of Adam? Yahya informed me of it, from al-Thawri."
"9451","9424 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ismail ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman conversed at night with al-Walid ibn Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt, then they left him and stood talking until they saw the first signs of dawn. Then each one of them prayed the witr with one rakah."
"9452","9425 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: Abdullah would recite in the last rakah of the witr: Say, He is Allah, the One, then he would raise his hands and say the qunut before bowing."
"9453","9426 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Aban, from al-Nakhai, that Ibn Masud would say the qunut throughout the year in the witr."
"9454","9427 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from more than one of the companions of Abdullah: that Ibn Masud would say: When one of you prays the witr then sleeps and then stands, let him undo his witr, and pray another rakah added to it, then pray the witr after that."
"9455","9428 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah ibn Qays, that Ibn Masud would not say the qunut in the Fajr prayer."
"9456","9429 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, that Ibn Masud would not say the qunut in the morning prayer."
"9457","9430 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Abu al-Umays narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to me, he said: Abdullah would not say the qunut in the morning prayer, and when he said the qunut in the witr, he said it before bowing."
"9458","9431 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud would not say the qunut in the morning prayer."
"9459","9432 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad narrated, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibn Masud, that he would say the qunut in the witr before bowing, and would not say the qunut in the Fajr prayer."
"9460","9433 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Abu Ishaq, that al-Walid ibn Uqbah sent to Hudhayfah and Ibn Masud asking them about the prayer on the day of Eid. Then the Fajr prayer was established, so Ibn Masud stood behind a pillar and prayed two rakahs, then he joined them."
"9461","9434 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that it was grievous to him to hear anyone speaking after the break of dawn until the morning prayer is prayed."
"9462","9435 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that he disliked talking when he had prayed the two rakahs before the Fajr."
"9463","9436 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, he said: It was grievous to Abdullah ibn Masud to speak after the Fajr except with the remembrance of Allah."
"9464","9437 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: There was no hour among the hours harder upon Ibn Masud to hear someone speaking in it than from the splitting of dawn until the rising of the sun."
"9465","9438 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Ibn Masud went out to a people talking after the Fajr, and he forbade them from talking, and said: You have come only for the prayer, so either pray or be silent."
"9466","9439 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn al-Taymi, from Layth, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Masud passed by two men talking after the break of dawn, and said: O you two, either pray or be silent."
"9467","9440 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud disliked talking when he had prayed the two rakahs of Fajr."
"9468","9441 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: The daytime prayer of Abdullah was four before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, two before Fajr, and he would not pray before Asr nor after it."
"9469","9442 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: The voluntary prayer of Abdullah which he would not leave was: four before Zuhr and two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Subh."
"9470","9443 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: The voluntary prayer of Abdullah from which he would not reduce was four before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before the morning prayer."
"9471","9444 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: The prayer of Abdullah which he would not abandon was four before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."
"9472","9445 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from Shuayb ibn Khalid, from Abu Ishaq Abdullah ibn Budayl, the most intimate of people with Abdullah ibn Masud narrated to me, that he would say: When the sun declined he would stand and bow four rakahs, reciting in them two surahs from the Miin. When the muezzins called to one another he would tighten his clothes upon him, then go out to the prayer."
"9473","9446 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, Murrah and Masruq, they said: Abdullah said: Nothing of the daytime prayer equals the night prayer except four before Zuhr, and their excellence over the daytime prayer is like the excellence of the congregational prayer over the prayer of the individual."
"9474","9447 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from Abu Ubaydah, that his father would not pray the Duha prayer."
"9475","9448 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: There is an hour in which I never came to him but that I found him standing praying between Maghrib and Isha, meaning Abdullah ibn Masud."
"9476","9449 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: There is an hour in which I never came to Abdullah ibn Masud but that I found him praying in it, between Maghrib and Isha. So I asked Abdullah and said: There is an hour in which I never came to you but that I found you praying. He said: It is an hour of heedlessness."
"9477","9450 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father al-Aswad ibn Yazid, he said: Abdullah said: The best hour of heedlessness, meaning the prayer between Maghrib and Isha."
"9478","9451 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Ghassan al-Nahdi narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: Drowsiness at fighting is security from Allah, and drowsiness in prayer is from Satan."
"9479","9452 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Asim, from Abu Razin, he said: Abdullah said: Drowsiness in prayer is from Satan, and drowsiness in fighting is security from Allah."
"9480","9453 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abu Zibyan, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Yawning and sneezing in prayer are from Satan."
"9481","9454 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Ibn Masud said: The prayer is not shortened except in Hajj or jihad."
"9482","9455 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Khusayf al-Jazari narrated, Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that he said: Do not reduce any of your prayer in your outlying stations nor in your encampments, and do not travel to the villages of the Sawad for your needs and say: We are travelers. The traveler is only one who goes from horizon to horizon."
"9483","9456 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Khusayf, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Masud, that he said: Do not be deceived by your trading journeys and your encampments, traveling to the villages of the Sawad and saying: We are travelers. The traveler is only one who goes from horizon to horizon."
"9484","9457 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: Do not be deceived by your sawaad, for the encampment of one of you with his family is one thing, unless he be compelled."
"9485","9458 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, the same as that."
"9486","9459 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ghalib ibn Ubayd Allah, Hammad informed me, from Ibrahim, that Ibn Masud said: Whoever prays four in travel repeats the prayer."
"9487","9460 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah was asked about a man who lays his side down at the two rakahs of Duha? He said: What is with one of you that he wallows like the wallowing of the donkey."
"9488","9461 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from al-Amash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, he said: We would sit in the mosque after Abdullah ibn Masud had stood, confirming the people in recitation. When we wanted to return we would pray two rakahs. That reached Abdullah ibn Masud, so he said: Do you burden the people with what Allah does not burden them with? They see you praying and regard that as obligatory upon them. If you must do it, then do it in the houses."
"9489","9462 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Muslim, from Masruq, he said: When Abdullah would stand we would sit after him, confirming the people in recitation. When we stood we prayed. That reached him, so we entered upon him and he said: Do you burden the people with what they are not burdened with? They see you and think it is sunnah. If you must do it, then do it in your houses. Sulayman said: Amr ibn Murrah also narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah."
"9490","9463 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, that Ibn Masud said: When Satan sees the son of Adam prostrating he shouts and says: Woe to him, woe to Satan. Allah commanded the son of Adam to prostrate and for him is Paradise, so he obeyed; and He commanded me to prostrate and I disobeyed, so for me is the Fire."
"9491","9464 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, that a man, while he was watering his crop, saw a cloud in a thicket and heard in it a voice: Water the land of so-and-so. So he followed the voice until he reached the land that was named. He asked its owner: What is your practice in it? He said: I return a third in it, give a third in charity, and keep a third for my family."
"9492","9465 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from al-Nakhai, from Masruq, that Ibn Masud used to send him to his land to do that in it."
"9493","Chapter. 9466 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah said: May Allah curse the tattooing women, the women who seek tattooing, the women who create gaps between teeth for beauty, altering the creation of Allah. That reached a woman from Banu Asad called Umm Yaqub. She said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, it reached me that you cursed such and such. He said: Why should I not curse whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed, and who is in the Book of Allah? She said: I read what is between the two covers and I do not find it. He said: If you had read, you would have found it. Have you not read: Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain. She said: Yes. He said: For the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it. She said: I think your family do some of that. He said: Go and look. So she entered and saw none of what she sought. Abdullah said: Had she been so, she would not have stayed with us. Al-Dabari said: We said to Abu Bakr: What is al-namisah? He said: She who plucks her hair."
"9494","9467 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: Cursed are the women who pluck eyebrows, who create gaps between teeth, and who seek tattooing. Shall I not curse whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed? A woman from Banu Asad said to him: I think it is in your family. He said: Go and look. So she went, then she came and said: I saw nothing in them, and I did not see it in the Mushaf. Abdullah said to her: Rather the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said it."
"9495","9468 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf al-Ammi narrated, my father narrated, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda, that a woman came to Ibn Masud and said: I am a woman with thin hair; is it right for me to join other hair to my hair? He said: No. She said: Is it something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or do you find it in the Book of Allah? He said: Rather I heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I find it in the Book of Allah. She said: By Allah, I have read what is between the two covers of the Mushaf and I did not find it. He said: Do you not find in it: Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain. She said: Yes. She said: By Allah, I see the one in your house doing it. He said: Then I would not have kept the counsel of my brother Shuayb. He said: So I adjure you to enter to her and look at her hair. So she entered and looked at a bald woman, and saw nothing in her hair. She went out and said: I found nothing. He said: Then I would not have kept the counsel of Shuayb."
"9496","9469 - Muhammad ibn Jarir al-Tabari the jurist narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Man narrated, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: Abdullah said: May Allah curse the women who create gaps between teeth, the women who pluck eyebrows, and the women who seek tattooing, altering the creation of Allah. A woman from Banu Asad called Umm al-Mustawrid came to him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, it reached me that you cursed the women who create gaps, the women who pluck, and the women who seek tattooing. He said: Shall I not curse whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed, and which is in the Book of Allah? She said: I have read what is between the two covers and I did not find it in it. He said: If you had read what is between the two covers, it is indeed in the Book of Allah: Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain. She said: By Allah, I think your family do it. He said: Enter and look; if they do it, they shall not spend a night with me. So she entered and looked, then she went out saying: I saw nothing, I saw nothing."
"9497","9470 - Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from Asim al-Ahwal, he said: I heard Azrah saying: Abu al-Aliyah said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: Cursed are the woman who joins hair, the tattooing woman, the woman who creates a gap, and the woman who plucks. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said it."
"9498","9471 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, that Abdullah ibn Masud said: By Him besides whom there is no god, no woman ever prayed a prayer better for her than a prayer she prays in her house, except that it be the Sacred Mosque, or the mosque of the Messenger, except an old woman in her manqalayn."
"9499","9472 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Ibn Masud, he said: A woman never prayed in a place better for her than her house, except that it be the Sacred Mosque, or the mosque of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except a woman who goes out in her manqalayn, meaning her two khuffs."
"9500","9473 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from his father, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: I heard the master of this house swearing and stressing the oath: There is no prayer place of a woman better for her than her house, except in Hajj or Umrah, except a woman who has despaired of husbands, for she is in her manqalayn. I said: What is her manqalayn? He said: An old woman whose steps have become short."
"9501","9474 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Said ibn Masruq narrated, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: Abdullah swore and stressed the oath: There is no prayer place for a woman better than her house, except in Hajj or Umrah, except a woman who has despaired of husbands, for she is in her manqalayn."
"9502","9475 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, that he saw Ibn Masud expelling the women from the mosque on Friday, saying: Go out to your houses; it is better for you."
"9503","9476 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Shubah narrated, Abu Ishaq informed me, Abu Amr al-Shaybani informed me, he said: I saw Ibn Masud driving the women out of the mosque on Friday."
"9504","9477 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Ibn Masud, that he would drive the women out of the mosque on Friday, saying: Pray in your houses."
"9505","9478 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: A woman never did anything better than sitting in the bottom of her house worshipping her Lord. One of them says: I will go to my family, then Satan looks eagerly at her until she says: No one saw me but that I pleased him."
"9506","9479 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: Women are but awrah. A woman leaves her house while there is nothing wrong with her, then Satan looks eagerly at her and says: You will not pass by anyone but that you will please him. A woman puts on her clothes and it is said: Where do you intend? She says: I visit a sick person, attend a funeral, or pray in a mosque. No woman ever worshipped her Lord with anything like worshipping Him in her house."
"9507","9480 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Abu Hilal narrated, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, he said: A woman is awrah. When she leaves her house, Satan looks eagerly at her, so she says: No one saw me but that I pleased him. The closest she is to Allah is when she is in the bottom of her house."
"9508","9481 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, he said: The prayer of a woman in her house is better than her prayer in her chamber, her prayer in her chamber is better than her prayer in her courtyard, and her prayer in her courtyard is better than her prayer elsewhere. Then he said: When a woman goes out, Satan looks eagerly at her."
"9509","9482 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, he said: The prayer of a woman in the house is better than her prayer in the courtyard, and her prayer in the courtyard is better than her prayer outside it."
"9510","9483 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Mamar, from Ibn Masud, he said: The men and women among the Children of Israel used to pray together. When a woman had a lover, she would wear the two wooden pattens, lengthening herself with them for her lover. So Allah cast menstruation upon them. Ibn Masud would say: Put them back where Allah put them back. We said to Abu Bakr: What are al-qalabayn? He said: Two dancing boards of wood."
"9511","9484 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah, he said: A woman among the Children of Israel would wear the two wooden pattens and stand upon them, then promise her lover. So menstruation was cast upon them. Abdullah would say: Put them back where Allah put them back."
"9512","Chapter. 9485 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Husayn, from Abd al-Ala, he said: I entered the mosque with Ibn Masud and he bowed. A man passed by him while he was bowing and greeted him, so he said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. When he finished, he said: It was said: Among the signs of the Hour are that a man greets a man only for acquaintance, mosques are taken as thoroughfares, women and horses become expensive, then they become cheap and do not become expensive again until the Day of Resurrection, and a man and a woman trade together."
"9513","9486 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Husayn narrated, from Abd al-Ala ibn al-Hakam al-Kalbi, from Kharijah ibn al-Salt al-Burjumi, he said: We came to the mosque with Abdullah ibn Masud, and Abdullah said: It was said: Among the nearness of the Hour is that mosques are taken as thoroughfares."
"9514","9487 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, he said: Ibn Masud entered the mosque and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the signs of the Hour is that a man passes through the length and breadth of the mosque without praying two rakahs in it. Thus Mansur narrated it, and Qatadah joined it."
"9515","9488 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his father, he said: Ibn Masud met a man who said: Peace be upon you, O Ibn Masud. Ibn Masud said: Allah and His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Among the signs of the Hour is that a man passes through the mosque without praying two rakahs in it, a man greets only whom he knows, and a boy sends an old man as a courier."
"9516","9489 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Umar ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Maymun Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: A Bedouin met Abdullah ibn Masud while we were with him, and said: Peace be upon you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He laughed and said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The Hour will not come until greeting is upon acquaintance, mosques are taken as thoroughfares so that no prostration to Allah is made in them, a boy sends an old man as a courier between the two horizons, and a trader reaches between the two horizons without finding profit."
"9517","9490 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated, Mujalid narrated, from al-Shabi, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, he said: The prayer was established in the mosque, so we came walking with Abdullah. When the people bowed, Abdullah bowed, and we bowed with him while walking. A man passed before him and said: Peace be upon you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. Abdullah said while bowing: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. When he finished, some of the people asked him: Why did you say when the man greeted you, Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Among the signs of the Hour is when greeting is upon acquaintance."
"9518","9491 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from Qays, he said: Abdullah would say: Perform this prayer well, and shorten these sermons."
"9519","9492 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, he said: Length of prayer and shortness of sermon are a sign of a man's understanding."
"9520","9493 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, he said: Length of prayer and shortness of sermon are a sign of a man's understanding."
"9521","9494 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: There will be rulers over you who kill the prayer. Whoever among you reaches that, let him pray it at its time, and make his prayer with them supererogatory."
"9522","9495 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, he said: You are in a time whose speakers are few and whose scholars are many. They lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon. A time will come upon you whose speakers are many and whose scholars are few. They will lengthen the sermon and delay the prayer, until it is said: This is the sharqu al-mawta. I said to him: What is sharqu al-mawta? He said: When the sun has become very yellow. Whoever among you reaches that, let him pray the prayer at its time. If he is detained, let him pray with them, making his prayer alone the obligation and his prayer with them voluntary."
"9523","9496 - Al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Ammar, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Abdullah, he said: There will be rulers who abandon of the Sunnah like this. If you abandon it, they will make it like this. If you abandon it, they will bring the great calamity."
"9524","9497 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Husayn, from al-Shabi, from Mahdi, he said: Ibn Masud said: How will you be, O Mahdi, when your best appear and your youngest, or your worst, are employed over you, and prayer is prayed at other than its appointed time? I said: I do not know. He said: Do not be a tax-collector, nor a headman, nor a policeman, nor a courier, and pray the prayer at its appointed time."
"9525","9498 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah would pray with them when they delayed it a little, holding that they bear the sin of that."
"9526","9499 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Al-Walid ibn Uqbah delayed the prayer, so Ibn Masud ordered the muezzin who called the prayer. Then he stepped forward and led the people. Al-Walid sent to him: What did you do? Did news come to you from the Commander of the Faithful, or did you innovate? Ibn Masud said: Neither of that happened. Allah and His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not command us to wait for you with our prayer while you attend to your need."
"9527","9500 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Ibn Masud, that he said: Among harshness are four: that one hears the muezzin saying: Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest; I bear witness there is no god but Allah, I bear witness there is no god but Allah, yet does not say like what he says; that one wipes his face before finishing his prayer; that one urinates standing; and that one prays with nothing between him and the qiblah screening him."
"9528","9501 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Asim, from al-Musayyab, raising the hadith to Abdullah, he said: Four are of harshness: that a man hears the muezzin magnifying Allah yet does not magnify, and he testifies yet he does not testify; that he wipes his forehead of dust while praying; and that he prays in open land with no sutrah between him and the qiblah."
"9529","9502 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sharik narrated, from Asim, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Abdullah, he said: Four are of harshness: that you wipe your face while in prayer; that you pray toward other than a sutrah; that you urinate standing; and that you hear the muezzin yet do not say as he says."
"9530","9503 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: A man came to Abdullah and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose. Abdullah said to him: Perform wudu in the best manner you would perform wudu, and pray in the best manner you would pray. He thought that Abdullah had not understood from the enormity of what he brought. He returned and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose. Abdullah said to him: Perform wudu in the best manner you would perform wudu, and pray in the best manner you would pray. He fell silent until, when those with him became few, he said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose. Abdullah took his finger and squeezed it, then said: It was said to you only that you may understand: perform wudu in the best manner you would perform wudu, and pray in the best manner you would pray."
"9531","9504 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah and Yahya ibn al-Ala, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: A man came to Ibn Masud, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Zaidah."
"9532","9505 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: A man prays in two garments. So I met Ubayy ibn Kab and informed him. He said: Do all of you find two garments? He prays in one garment."
"9533","9506 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud and Aishah would perform voluntary prayer in travel before the prayer and after it."
"9534","9507 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from Abd al-Malik al-Awar, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, that Hudhayfah said to Ibn Masud: Do you not wonder at a people between your house and the house of Abu Musa who claim they are in itikaf? He said: Perhaps they are right and you are wrong."
"9535","9508 - Ali narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that Hudhayfah said to Ibn Masud: Do you not wonder at a people between your house and the house of Abu Musa who claim they are in itikaf? He said: Perhaps they are right and you are wrong, or they remembered and you forgot. He said: As for me, I knew that there is no itikaf except in a congregational mosque."
"9536","9509 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated; and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Ibrahim, he said: Hudhayfah came to Abdullah and said: Shall I not make you wonder at people devoted between your house and the house of al-Ashari? Abdullah said: Perhaps they are right and you are wrong. Hudhayfah said: I do not care whether I do itikaf in it or in this market of yours. Itikaf is only in these three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the mosque of Madinah, and the mosque of al-Aqsa. And those who had done itikaf, whom Hudhayfah blamed, were in the grand mosque of Kufa."
"9537","9510 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Jami ibn Abi Rashid, he said: I heard Abu Wail saying: Hudhayfah said to Abdullah: People devoted between your house and the house of Abu Musa, will you not forbid them? Abdullah said to him: Perhaps they are right and you are wrong, and they remembered and you forgot. Hudhayfah said: There is no itikaf except in these three mosques: the mosque of Madinah, the mosque of Makkah, and the mosque of Iliya."
"9538","9511 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated; and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Shaddad ibn al-Azma, he said: A man did itikaf in his tent, so the people pelted him. The man sent to Abdullah ibn Masud, so Abdullah came, drove the people away, and approved that."
"9539","9512 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Kurdus, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud would say the takbir in Adha and Fitr nine and nine. He would begin and say four, then recite, then say one and bow with it. Then he would stand in the other rakah, begin and recite, then say four, bowing with one of them."
"9540","9513 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, from Ashath, from Kurdus, he said: Al-Walid sent to Abdullah ibn Masud, Hudhayfah, Abu Masud and Abu Musa al-Ashari after the night prayer, saying: This is the Eid of the Muslims, so how is the prayer? They said: Ask Abu Abd al-Rahman. So he asked him, and he said: He stands and says four, then recites the Fatihat al-Kitab and a surah from the Mufassal, then says and bows. That is five. Then he stands and recites the Fatihat al-Kitab and a surah from the Mufassal, then says four, bowing in the last of them. That is nine in the two Eids. Not one of them denied it."
"9541","9514 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that al-Walid ibn Uqbah entered the mosque while Ibn Masud, Hudhayfah and Abu Musa were in the courtyard of the mosque. Al-Walid said: The Eid has come, so what shall I do? Ibn Masud said: You say: Allah is greatest, praise Allah, extol Him, send blessings upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and supplicate Allah. Then you say takbir, praise Allah, extol Him, send blessings upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then you say takbir, praise Allah, extol Him, send blessings upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and supplicate Allah. Then you say takbir, praise Allah, extol Him, send blessings upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and supplicate. Then say takbir, recite the Fatihat al-Kitab and a surah, then say takbir, bow and prostrate. Then stand, recite the Fatihat al-Kitab and a surah, then say takbir, praise Allah, extol Him, send blessings upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and supplicate. Then say takbir, praise Allah, extol Him, send blessings upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bow and prostrate. He said: Hudhayfah and Abu Musa said: He is right."
"9542","9515 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah and al-Aswad ibn Yazid, they said: Ibn Masud was sitting, and with him were Hudhayfah and Abu Musa. Said ibn al-As asked them about the takbir in the prayer on the day of Fitr and Adha. Each one kept saying: Ask this, and this one saying: Ask this, until Hudhayfah said to him: Ask this, meaning Abdullah ibn Masud. So he asked him, and Ibn Masud said: He says four, then recites, then says takbir and bows. Then in the second he says takbir and recites, then says four after the recitation."
"9543","9516 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah and al-Aswad ibn Yazid, that Ibn Masud would say the takbir in the two Eids nine: four before the recitation, then he would say takbir and bow; and in the second he would recite, and when he finished he would say four, then bow."
"9544","9517 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from al-Aswad, Alqamah and Masruq, from Abdullah, that he would say nine takbirs in Adha and Fitr. He would stand and say four, then recite, then say one and bow with it. Then he would stand and recite, and say four, bowing with one."
"9545","9518 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Alqamah ibn Qays and from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Ibn Masud, that he would say in the first five takbirs with the takbir of bowing and the takbir of opening, and in the other four with the takbir of bowing."
"9546","9519 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, Abdullah ibn Abi Musa narrated to us, from his father, when Said ibn al-As called them: he called Abu Musa, Hudhayfah and Abdullah ibn Masud at dawn before praying the morning prayer, and asked them about the takbir on the day of Eid. Hudhayfah said: Ask al-Ashari. Al-Ashari said: Ask Abdullah, for he is the most knowledgeable of us and the earliest of us. So he asked him, and he said: You open with four, seal with four, say one takbir, then add to it three. Then you say takbir and bow. When you rise from the prostration you recite, then say four, then bow."
"9547","9520 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Atiyyah, from Abdullah, he said: The takbir in the two Eids is four, like the prayer over the dead."
"9548","9521 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abd al-Karim informed me, from al-Nakhai, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Ibn Masud, he said: Between every two takbirs is the measure of a word."
"9549","9522 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, that Ibn Masud and Hudhayfah would forbid the people, or he said: make sit, whomever they saw praying before the emergence of the imam on Eid."
"9550","9523 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad, that Ibn Masud and Hudhayfah would forbid the people on the day of Eid from praying before the emergence of the imam."
"9551","9524 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Hisham, from Muhammad, he said: I was informed that Ibn Masud and Hudhayfah would stand on Sacrifice and Fitr, forbidding anyone to pray before the imam."
"9552","9525 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated, I was informed that Ibn Masud and Hudhayfah, one of them or both: he stood up and forbade the people from praying on the day of Eid before the emergence of the imam."
"9553","9526 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Ibn Masud would not pray before it, and would pray after it four rakahs."
"9554","9527 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin and Qatadah, that Ibn Masud would pray after it four rakahs or eight, and would not pray before it."
"9555","9528 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Salih, from al-Shabi, he said: Ibn Masud would pray after the two Eids four."
"9556","9529 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Hurayth, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that he would pray after the Eid four."
"9557","9530 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: Whoever misses the Eid, let him pray four."
"9558","9531 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Sufyan, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: Whoever misses the Eid, let him pray four."
"9559","9532 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Barrah al-Sanani narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated, al-Thawri informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Ibn Masud, that he would say the takbir from the morning prayer on the day of Arafah until the Asr prayer of the day of Sacrifice."
"9560","9533 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah informed me, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Ibn Masud, concerning Zakat al-Fitr, he said: A mudd of wheat, or a sa of dates or barley."
"9561","9534 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr al-Taymi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: I bathed with Ibn Masud on the day of Arafah under the arak tree."
"9562","9535 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Shubah narrated, al-Hakam and Hammad informed me, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah would say: The takbir in the days of Tashriq is after the Subh prayer from the day of Arafah until after the Asr of the day of Sacrifice."
"9563","9536 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from the companions of Abdullah, from Abdullah, that he would say the takbir from the morning prayer of the day of Arafah, and stop at the Asr prayer of the day of Sacrifice, saying takbir when he had prayed Asr. He said: And he would say takbir: Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest; there is no god but Allah; and Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest, and to Allah belongs praise."
"9564","9537 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: When the call is made for prayer on Friday, hasten to the remembrance of Allah. Abdullah said: Had I read it: hasten, I would have hastened until my cloak fell. And he would read it: proceed."
"9565","9538 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: In the reading of Ibn Masud: proceed to the remembrance of Allah, and it is like His saying: Indeed your striving is diverse."
"9566","9539 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Hammad informed us, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, that he asked Ubayy ibn Kab, while the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was delivering the sermon, about a verse from the Book of Allah, but he turned away from him and did not answer him. When he finished his prayer, he said: You did not attend Jumuah. Ibn Masud asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Ubayy spoke the truth."
"9567","9540 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir al-Bajali narrated, from Ibrahim, he said: A man asked Abdullah ibn Masud to recite while the imam was delivering the sermon on Friday, but Abdullah did not speak to him. When he finished the prayer, Abdullah said to him: What you asked about is your share of Jumuah."
"9568","9541 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi al-Fazari narrated, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: It suffices as idle talk that you say to your companion: Be silent, when the imam comes out on Friday."
"9569","9542 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, he said: I prayed, I and Zirr, and he led me, and we missed Jumuah. So I asked Ibrahim, and he said: Abdullah did that with Alqamah and al-Aswad. Sufyan said: And perhaps I and al-Amash did it."
"9570","9543 - Al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: Whoever catches one rakah of Jumuah, let him add to it another; and whoever misses the two rakahs, let him pray four."
"9571","9544 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, he said: Whoever catches the rakah has caught the Jumuah, and whoever does not catch the rakah, let him pray four."
"9572","9545 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Sabii was asked: Did you mention, from Abu al-Ahwas, that Abdullah said: Whoever catches the two rakahs or one of them has caught the Jumuah, and whoever misses both rakahs, let him pray four? He said: Yes."
"9573","9546 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: Whoever catches the sermon, then the Jumuah is two rakahs, and whoever does not catch it, let him pray four; and whoever does not catch the rakah, let him not count the prostration until he catches the rakah."
"9574","9547 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ibn Masud, he said: Whoever misses the last rakah, let him pray four. Mamar said: Qatadah said: He prays four. It was said to Qatadah: Ibn Masud came while they were sitting at the end of the prayer and said to his companions: Sit, you have caught it, if Allah wills. Qatadah said: He only means: You have caught the reward."
"9575","9548 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud used to teach us to pray four rakahs after the Jumuah, until we heard the saying of Ali: Pray six. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: So we pray six. Ata said: Abu Abd al-Rahman prays two rakahs, then four."
"9576","9549 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: Ibn Masud used to command us to pray four before the Jumuah and four after it, until Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came and commanded us to pray two after it, then four."
"9577","9550 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, he said: Ibn Masud used to command us to pray four before the Jumuah and four after it, until Ali came and commanded us to pray two after it, then four."
"9578","9551 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, he said: Ibn Masud commanded us to pray four after the Jumuah. He said: When Ali came he said: Make them six."
"9579","9552 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Qays, that Ibn Masud prayed on Friday, after the imam gave the salutation, four rakahs."
"9580","9553 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, that Ibn Masud used to pray four rakahs before the Jumuah and four rakahs after it. Abu Ishaq said: And Ali used to pray six rakahs after the Jumuah."
"9581","9554 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud used to pray four after the Jumuah."
"9582","9555 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, Zayd ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: We used to pray the Jumuah with Abdullah, then we would return and take the midday rest."
"9583","9556 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: We used to perform the Jumuah with Ibn Masud, then we would return and take the midday rest."
"9584","9557 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: I saw Abdullah ibn Masud patrolling the mosque at night; he would not see a dark figure in it but he would remove him, except a man standing in prayer."
"9585","9558 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Qays, he said: I heard Huzayl ibn Shurahbil say: Ibn Masud came to our mosque while the prayer had been announced, and it was said to him: Come forward. He said: Let your imam come forward. We said: Our imam is not here. He said: Let a man from among you come forward. So a man came forward and stood on a bench in the qiblah of the mosque, and Abdullah forbade him."
"9586","9559 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, that he disliked leading them in prayer from the elevated place."
"9587","9560 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Shaddad ibn Maqil, he said: Abdullah said: The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, and the last that will remain is prayer; and a people with no religion will indeed pray."
"9588","9561 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, Alqamah, and Masruq, that Abdullah said: Fasting is from the sighting of the crescent to its sighting; if it is hidden from you, then thirty days."
"9589","9562 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Utbah ibn Ammar informed us, from Ibn Ayyash, from his father, he said: I came to Abdullah ibn Masud and said: Some people of the quarter and some of our neighbors fasted today. He said: Upon sighting the crescent? He said: No. He said: That I break fast a day of Ramadan then make it up is dearer to me than that I fast a day of Shaban."
"9590","9563 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Jami ibn Shaddad, Abdullah ibn Mirdas narrated to us, he said: A man from the quarter came to me and said: I passed by my wife in the moonlight and she pleased me, so I had intercourse with her in the month of Ramadan, then I slept until morning. I said: Go to Abdullah ibn Masud or Abu Hakim al-Muzani. And there was Abdullah ibn Masud, so I asked him and said: I was in a state of major impurity. He said: You were in a state of major impurity in which prayer was not lawful for you; then you washed, so prayer became lawful for you, and fasting became lawful for you, so fast."
"9591","9564 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: I heard Jami ibn Shaddad Abu Sakhrah narrating, from Abdullah ibn Mirdas, that he came to the mosque of the quarter after they had prayed Fajr, and said to them - and that was in Ramadan: I went to my wife, then sleep overcame me, so morning came and I had not washed; what do you think? The people said to him: We see nothing but that you have broken your fast. So he went to Abdullah ibn Masud, who said to them: You have come to one better than you, or more understanding. He said: Breaking fast is only from food and drink, so complete your fast."
"9592","9565 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, Jami ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, he said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Masud and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I was in a state of major impurity and did not wash until morning. Abdullah said: You were in a state of major impurity in which prayer was not lawful for you; then you washed, so prayer became lawful for you, and fasting became lawful for you. And that was in Ramadan."
"9593","9566 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin said: Yahya ibn al-Jazzar narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: If I went to my wife at night, then deliberately left the washing until morning, it would not prevent me from fasting; I only went to her while she was lawful to me."
"9594","9567 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, that Ibn Masud said: If I went to my wife at night, then deliberately left the washing until morning, that would not prevent me from fasting, because I only went to her while she was lawful to me."
"9595","9568 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ayyub and Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that Ibn Masud said: If I went to my family at the beginning of the night, then morning came while I was in a state of major impurity, I would fast, because I went to her while she was lawful to me."
"9596","9569 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: If I were in a state of major impurity and remained a month without finding water, I would not pray until I find water."
"9597","9570 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from al-Hurmuzan, from Ibn Masud, concerning a man who kisses while fasting, he said: He makes up a day in its place. Sufyan said: This is not acted upon."
"9598","9571 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Zakariyya, from al-Shabi, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, that Ibn Masud used to touch his wife affectionately at midday while he was fasting."
"9599","9572 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri, from a man, he said: Ibn Masud said: Whoever breaks fast a day of Ramadan without an excuse will meet Allah with it, even if he fasts the whole year; if He wills He forgives him, and if He wills He punishes him."
"9600","9573 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, he said: Abdullah said: Whoever breaks fast a day of Ramadan... and he mentioned the like."
